enal acid–base compensation is slower.","D":"Respiratory CO2 changes alter blood pH within minutes, whereas renal acid–base compensation is slower."},"references":[],"review":"new_independent_provisional_answer_manual_fact_reasoning","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"2eb4da217bde32909e98e2c8b7bd27067a07be724c69fde7f3e0bebdbfaf33c1"},"q-1c636dcf9a74":{"correct":"C","answerText":"tertiary structure","explanation":"Tertiary structure describes overall three-dimensional folding of an individual polypeptide chain.","optionReasons":{"A":"This choice does not fit the key distinction in the question. Tertiary structure describes overall three-dimensional folding of an individual polypeptide chain.","B":"This choice does not fit the key distinction in the question. Tertiary structure describes overall three-dimensional folding of an individual polypeptide chain.","C":"Tertiary structure describes overall three-dimensional folding of an individual polypeptide chain.","D":"This choice does not fit the key distinction in the question. Tertiary structure describes overall three-dimensional folding of an individual polypeptide chain."},"references":[],"review":"new_independent_provisional_answer_manual_fact_reasoning","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"fd7063178c70b64bb5d2ca92673dc5ba234a865cf0542ee89b9ea05afd5f110f"},"q-d2751421781a":{"correct":"A","answerText":"spindle fibres pull each chromatid to opposite sides of the cell","explanation":"During anaphase, sister chromatids separate and move toward opposite spindle poles.","optionReasons":{"A":"During anaphase, sister chromatids separate and move toward opposite spindle poles.","B":"This choice does not fit the key distinction in the question. During anaphase, sister chromatids separate and move toward opposite spindle poles.","C":"This choice does not fit the key distinction in the question. During anaphase, si