of bovine abortion; infected cows may otherwise show few clinical signs."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"1fe187cd68384e7897b55d028cf8ae70a9d6a29aac06353b61247b2f3fbc6e3b"},"q-2b3ce07db6f9":{"correct":"E","answerText":"a and b","explanation":"Both Encephalitozoon cuniculi and Baylisascaris procyonis can cause neurologic disease including abnormal posture or ataxia in rabbits.","optionReasons":{"E":"Both Encephalitozoon cuniculi and Baylisascaris procyonis can cause neurologic disease including abnormal posture or ataxia in rabbits."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"603a652c79307d837cf03dca1ddf806e22cd8dcbd0e0072acf8909a5a4fbf0e0"},"q-ee1a7732b973":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Fresh frozen plasma.","explanation":"Fresh frozen plasma contains multiple coagulation factors and is appropriate when bleeding is associated with significant acquired clotting-factor deficiency; packed cells mainly provide oxygen-carrying capacity.","optionReasons":{"D":"Fresh frozen plasma contains multiple coagulation factors and is appropriate when bleeding is associated with significant acquired clotting-factor deficiency; packed cells mainly provide oxygen-carrying capacity."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"98a840a09c6c6af8e01a2fcf3480cf8539eb0f606a0d0c340cd67848c641f09f"},"q-a37d57d88c60":{"correct":"E","answerText":"Depression","explanation":"Hyperesthesia or increased intensity of perception can accompany migraine, stimulant or hallucinogen intoxication and mania; depression more often causes reduced sensory vividness.","optionReasons":{"E":"Hyperesthesia or increased intensity of perception can accompany migraine, stimulant or hallucinogen intoxication and mania; depression more often causes reduced sensory vividness."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"4d9d59aeb5c2d78f0fae2e452828652ea5ee98e0131b24cdbe45b1aa938c4a06"},"q-8d1a41a8850c":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Ego-dystonic","explanation":"An ego-dystonic thought feels alien or inconsistent with a person's values and is characteristic of many obsessions.","optionReasons":{"A":"An ego-dystonic thought feels alien or inconsistent with a person's values and is characteristic of many obsessions."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"6c6b791b63138ec407a1469a913f166011976186f308e215a214d6c6ded79373"},"q-4051e9bb6ff6":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Thought blocking","explanation":"Thought insertion, withdrawal and broadcasting involve loss of agency over thoughts; thought blocking is interruption in the flow of thinking.","optionReasons":{"D":"Thought insertion, withdrawal and broadcasting involve loss of agency over thoughts; thought blocking is interruption in the flow of thinking."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"548627555c3ae8811bbbf553050cb2c1466051c3e1d41ca60e3d1a1191a8d62d"},"q-4a4e8f630252":{"correct":"E","answerText":"Callousness","explanation":"Conviction, preoccupation, distress and impaired insight describe delusional belief dimensions; callousness does not.","optionReasons":{"E":"Conviction, preoccupation, distress and impaired insight describe delusional belief dimensions; callousness does not."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"37a5c01ddc653033e4b90cb190364ab24eb69530f4da62a30ea5afd422ab96ae"},"q-3c0805cb76c5":{"correct":"E","answerText":"Delusional misinterpretation","explanation":"Primary delusions can appear as intuition, delusional perception, mood or memory; a delusional misinterpretation is more usually a secondary explanation of an experience.","optionReasons":{"E":"Primary delusions can appear as intuition, delusional perception, mood or memory; a delusional misinterpretation is more usually a secondary explanation of an experience."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"b1bbf7987d03cf3de4361412c47459c92bc9b16fde9ecf42cdaec6eb6a6ae269"},"q-509b38075589":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Cotard’s syndrome","explanation":"Cotard syndrome is a nihilistic delusion, while Capgras, Fregoli, intermetamorphosis and reduplicative paramnesia are delusional misidentification syndromes.","optionReasons":{"B":"Cotard syndrome is a nihilistic delusion, while Capgras, Fregoli, intermetamorphosis and reduplicative paramnesia are delusional misidentification syndromes."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"db6316525c05feb3efb08119024d761c884b4ddb54b8238c5b8a9f1da21a0521"},"q-c95b16af5ab5":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Lack of genuine causal links in speech","explanation":"Asyndesis denotes breakdown of the normal logical or causal connections between ideas in speech.","optionReasons":{"A":"Asyndesis denotes breakdown of the normal logical or causal connections between ideas in speech."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"2f8c7296da52b08ae514d73ab5e6c363be6ddb8d4a7f787c37b9d35c10060afe"},"q-0321f7a952dc":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Overinclusion","explanation":"Overinclusive thinking includes irrelevant members within categories and can be assessed with sorting and classification tasks.","optionReasons":{"A":"Overinclusive thinking includes irrelevant members within categories and can be assessed with sorting and classification tasks."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"b4df1c3e66984e9ce336b78b319316459da8536daacd397da45e171a77807117"},"q-002b4f235d83":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Vorbeireden","explanation":"Vorbeireden describes approximate answers to simple questions despite understanding, as in the Ganser phenomenon.","optionReasons":{"A":"Vorbeireden describes approximate answers to simple questions despite understanding, as in the Ganser phenomenon."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"69ff951ccbf2e2d273725b8d33bb88d09902b6e5669cf1198abaf0a7324bb891"},"q-62aba936ab74":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Comprehension","explanation":"Pure word deafness impairs understanding spoken words despite relatively preserved ability to read, write or produce speech.","optionReasons":{"D":"Pure word deafness impairs understanding spoken words despite relatively preserved ability to read, write or produce speech."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"d42b97a314dc0b76fec559441cf299542c82842ce5f076c3b344fab17e067b27"},"q-7c75d398959a":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Déjà vu","explanation":"Déjà vu is an abnormal sense of familiarity with a novel experience, a disturbance of familiarity rather than memory fabrication.","optionReasons":{"A":"Déjà vu is an abnormal sense of familiarity with a novel experience, a disturbance of familiarity rather than memory fabrication."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"3e7031fc4bd08bf276338c029a067839e65e2e1d3aef38aaf91d6e8c5a3b2c15"},"q-ce66d07f2bb6":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Approximate answers","explanation":"Ganser syndrome is classically associated with approximate answers, in which a person answers near—but not exactly—the expected answer.","optionReasons":{"B":"Ganser syndrome is classically associated with approximate answers, in which a person answers near—but not exactly—the expected answer."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"f678f032e4f5334202d3f2cf414bf2ba4ba74531bfd8df6f0cae3bc329bddb2a"},"q-849215f01564":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Depersonalization","explanation":"Depersonalization is a subjective alteration of self-experience, often described as feeling 'as if' detached or unreal while insight is preserved.","optionReasons":{"C":"Depersonalization is a subjective alteration of self-experience, often described as feeling 'as if' detached or unreal while insight is preserved."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"0ef5ad6519fc0c776e6f6685fe58fa6249568136bd352a0fd5a1de194567f747"},"q-94f95289bfc7":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Impulse control symptoms","explanation":"Pathological gambling was historically classified among impulse-control disorders, characterized by difficulty resisting harmful urges.","optionReasons":{"C":"Pathological gambling was historically classified among impulse-control disorders, characterized by difficulty resisting harmful urges."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"6f89cfa23fd4589171db4a1cc30b509c6b8dc94f1df46fb67e53d24f44ea1030"},"q-4cacf67754b5":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Dissociation disorder","explanation":"Astasia–abasia is a striking difficulty standing or walking that may occur with functional (dissociative) neurological symptoms.","optionReasons":{"D":"Astasia–abasia is a striking difficulty standing or walking that may occur with functional (dissociative) neurological symptoms."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"9f6fe7d0cc3142918811fb8ed67492306ccd8e7236746412084bf89b687c9142"},"q-8faba2fcff04":{"correct":"E","answerText":"None of the above","explanation":"Hallucinations can arise with illness, sensory deprivation, sleep transitions or even occasionally in people without mental illness; none of the listed groups is incapable of experiencing them.","optionReasons":{"E":"Hallucinations can arise with illness, sensory deprivation, sleep transitions or even occasionally in people without mental illness; none of the listed groups is incapable of experiencing them."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"130453c937cee2fb353caaac47e3a318b24d1a3a1a1cf7b42ae36473b6bc4a7b"},"q-8b337e6405f3":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Preceding mental phenomenon","explanation":"Primary delusions arise without a readily understandable preceding psychological phenomenon; secondary delusions are related to antecedent mood, experience or another symptom.","optionReasons":{"A":"Primary delusions arise without a readily understandable preceding psychological phenomenon; secondary delusions are related to antecedent mood, experience or another symptom."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"b3b1b30b394dd3e2901e11b68bb14cd5689f04dba5d39844a1761fd3149513e9"},"q-ea2885ad647f":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Astasia–abasia","explanation":"Astasia–abasia is classically a functional gait disturbance, whereas posturing, negativism, ambitendence and mitgehen are catatonic phenomena.","optionReasons":{"D":"Astasia–abasia is classically a functional gait disturbance, whereas posturing, negativism, ambitendence and mitgehen are catatonic phenomena."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"45a527c6c7e252bd99b4ab092b570c2c7a064d1278e66c10d326d80608eef5ee"},"q-342beed1bdb9":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Two persons sharing delusional content","explanation":"Folie à deux refers to shared delusional beliefs between closely associated individuals, not merely two people with the same diagnosis.","optionReasons":{"C":"Folie à deux refers to shared delusional beliefs between closely associated individuals, not merely two people with the same diagnosis."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"d39cdd24dafd03f8fc9c23a22289c54b8aac13fdb8d4257a8d0c7cea4b5c11a7"},"q-cc23fd5f46eb":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Catastrophic reaction","explanation":"A catastrophic reaction is acute agitation or distress when a cognitively impaired patient faces a task beyond current abilities.","optionReasons":{"A":"A catastrophic reaction is acute agitation or distress when a cognitively impaired patient faces a task beyond current abilities."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"a27d13152514d1516f5c8ddec01eeb160fc3281d68ba2b0771e000d1ed7e8010"},"q-91bc7adbc9dd":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Autism","explanation":"Pronominal reversal, such as confusing 'I' and 'you', is a language phenomenon historically described in some autistic children.","optionReasons":{"D":"Pronominal reversal, such as confusing 'I' and 'you', is a language phenomenon historically described in some autistic children."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"0fb9529a5280c3c7e662a3439440a22294602c5ffd8d2b33ce962afa3d16173e"},"q-fa076265dd8f":{"correct":"D","answerText":"mitral stenosis","explanation":"Mitral stenosis primarily enlarges the left atrium and causes pulmonary venous hypertension, not the pressure-overload pattern of left ventricular hypertrophy.","optionReasons":{"D":"Mitral stenosis primarily enlarges the left atrium and causes pulmonary venous hypertension, not the pressure-overload pattern of left ventricular hypertrophy."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"94029acde8ef56c63a57052b5a18eb3cfdb7ba44bb4053ca99cc5040b26713ed"},"q-a94739100c78":{"correct":"A","answerText":"mitral stenosis","explanation":"Isolated mitral stenosis affects the left atrium and pulmonary circuit but does not usually produce left ventricular hypertrophy.","optionReasons":{"A":"Isolated mitral stenosis affects the left atrium and pulmonary circuit but does not usually produce left ventricular hypertrophy."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"694f28919fe51d5c6e378f4a557f3a7d9783f2adc44206e820ea88d00aa93f89"},"q-5d2694f59b43":{"correct":"C","answerText":"both","explanation":"Both severe aortic stenosis and coronary atherosclerotic disease can precipitate sudden unexpected cardiac death.","optionReasons":{"C":"Both severe aortic stenosis and coronary atherosclerotic disease can precipitate sudden unexpected cardiac death."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"1e1685947a0dc5ba0cc9a397526d27bf49a2816ee94423c3ce461993192b20f5"},"q-66212ea728b9":{"correct":"D","answerText":"aortic valvular disease","explanation":"Cor pulmonale arises from pulmonary vascular or parenchymal disease causing right-heart strain; aortic valve disease causes left-sided cardiac pathology.","optionReasons":{"D":"Cor pulmonale arises from pulmonary vascular or parenchymal disease causing right-heart strain; aortic valve disease causes left-sided cardiac pathology."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"ddd46282650ccefd16c0acc3bd83129c65a439c1cc8ba6c525709992aef64edf"},"q-20b9b43d5982":{"correct":"D","answerText":"pulmonary edema","explanation":"Cor pulmonale causes systemic venous congestion, including edema, hepatomegaly and raised jugular venous pressure; cardiogenic pulmonary edema is primarily left-sided.","optionReasons":{"D":"Cor pulmonale causes systemic venous congestion, including edema, hepatomegaly and raised jugular venous pressure; cardiogenic pulmonary edema is primarily left-sided."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"7eb2371a7e92a7de6008d23a401eaebc963ab588486bd46ea571f0a1e0f24f55"},"q-006d87a52356":{"correct":"D","answerText":"associated with stenosis of the pulmonic valve and a loud holosystolic murmur","explanation":"Cor pulmonale is right ventricular disease secondary to lung or pulmonary vascular pathology, not primary pulmonary-valve stenosis.","optionReasons":{"D":"Cor pulmonale is right ventricular disease secondary to lung or pulmonary vascular pathology, not primary pulmonary-valve stenosis."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"1068f6ef1d09ccb3e47470e3a0547cd7f18d9894a13aeff57abd1d33482eeef7"},"q-a13c2295b4dd":{"correct":"D","answerText":"ventricular septal defect","explanation":"Hemodynamically significant ventricular septal defects are often detected by childhood murmur or symptoms, whereas several other lesions may remain unnoticed until adulthood.","optionReasons":{"D":"Hemodynamically significant ventricular septal defects are often detected by childhood murmur or symptoms, whereas several other lesions may remain unnoticed until adulthood."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"135ece6a5ddd07592b1a0816594d8c4d47659ca7375caec3c2f3e1b68e4bda93"},"q-b1be73612c28":{"correct":"C","answerText":"tetralogy of Fallot","explanation":"Tetralogy of Fallot produces right-to-left shunting across a ventricular septal defect when right ventricular outflow is obstructed, causing cyanosis.","optionReasons":{"C":"Tetralogy of Fallot produces right-to-left shunting across a ventricular septal defect when right ventricular outflow is obstructed, causing cyanosis."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"2f78aad3d3cf9220a106d51e6c0f04ba007f7a73b96230870f56293972dca140"},"q-e7f46fb809aa":{"correct":"D","answerText":"ventricular septal defect","explanation":"Ventricular septal defect is the commonest congenital heart defect clinically recognized in childhood when isolated bicuspid aortic valve is excluded from the case definition.","optionReasons":{"D":"Ventricular septal defect is the commonest congenital heart defect clinically recognized in childhood when isolated bicuspid aortic valve is excluded from the case definition."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"3b293a994171d3c5f496f3448186c24bb98d4497b33047cde984a4a1ab7c086c"},"q-d9b67e32cb23":{"correct":"A","answerText":"atrial septal defect","explanation":"Tetralogy of Fallot comprises ventricular septal defect, right ventricular outflow obstruction, overriding aorta and right ventricular hypertrophy; atrial septal defect is not one of the four.","optionReasons":{"A":"Tetralogy of Fallot comprises ventricular septal defect, right ventricular outflow obstruction, overriding aorta and right ventricular hypertrophy; atrial septal defect is not one of the four."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"67e83306f06fc448b44537eead7a0b849ce8d94236836dbd8cabee958c9dd991"},"q-dff0e0126686":{"correct":"A","answerText":"a congenital lesion","explanation":"Pulmonary valve stenosis is most often congenital, resulting from abnormal valve development.","optionReasons":{"A":"Pulmonary valve stenosis is most often congenital, resulting from abnormal valve development."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"b23c0901d1bc671b08b6665ee1070a0cb674570eba819aac27ff77bb8ab366b2"},"q-87110fd1da6c":{"correct":"C","answerText":"tetralogy of Fallot","explanation":"Tetralogy of Fallot combines a large VSD with subpulmonary obstruction and an overriding aorta.","optionReasons":{"C":"Tetralogy of Fallot combines a large VSD with subpulmonary obstruction and an overriding aorta."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"8e5a3b5602353381ecd3bd65e5aeec31275b2a06042c741243196a63776921f2"},"q-fb5364842c7a":{"correct":"B","answerText":"ventricular septal defect","explanation":"A VSD permits right ventricular blood to cross to the left ventricle and aorta in tetralogy with pulmonary atresia; pulmonary flow then reaches collateral or ductal vessels.","optionReasons":{"B":"A VSD permits right ventricular blood to cross to the left ventricle and aorta in tetralogy with pulmonary atresia; pulmonary flow then reaches collateral or ductal vessels."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"68293b4baad705cba70d356dcaef8d8ed4dfe068639b1f4617a339b1d9e83a2f"},"q-57b9016c6a28":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Aschoff nodules","explanation":"Aschoff bodies are characteristic foci of rheumatic myocardial inflammation with activated macrophages and surrounding inflammatory cells.","optionReasons":{"A":"Aschoff bodies are characteristic foci of rheumatic myocardial inflammation with activated macrophages and surrounding inflammatory cells."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"b0205bba1c0e0f236b01b468a46f207af4b3eec7a506c53b7a22dc123a2742df"},"q-974321b35f6f":{"correct":"D","answerText":"verrucous endocarditis","explanation":"Acute rheumatic endocarditis produces small sterile verrucae along valve closure lines; destructive bacterial infection and chronic stenosis describe other processes.","optionReasons":{"D":"Acute rheumatic endocarditis produces small sterile verrucae along valve closure lines; destructive bacterial infection and chronic stenosis describe other processes."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"00bc1764fe3ae6ccd91d94a1c4787d6616f0246eee72ad89d4b21d71d6c42e3f"},"q-203e3e4e8092":{"correct":"B","answerText":"bacteria in heart valves","explanation":"Rheumatic fever follows an immune reaction to prior group A streptococcal infection, so bacteria usually are not present in affected valves.","optionReasons":{"B":"Rheumatic fever follows an immune reaction to prior group A streptococcal infection, so bacteria usually are not present in affected valves."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"6a195b7a7b6341463399dfd623aedd10fe0406e09d23904c908ecde92ff4b36a"},"q-bc90868b2912":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Group A beta-hemolytic streptococci","explanation":"Acute rheumatic fever can follow untreated pharyngitis caused by group A beta-hemolytic Streptococcus pyogenes.","optionReasons":{"B":"Acute rheumatic fever can follow untreated pharyngitis caused by group A beta-hemolytic Streptococcus pyogenes."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"64fbc49758b9f4c9a90361eb52c04825cd3137405a18b3fcaf6aaf1ad7af9c7d"},"q-475be2f2c824":{"correct":"A","answerText":"mitral valve","explanation":"Chronic rheumatic valve disease most often involves the mitral valve, alone or together with the aortic valve.","optionReasons":{"A":"Chronic rheumatic valve disease most often involves the mitral valve, alone or together with the aortic valve."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"e043fe4b85b56fff4ddc2a9b19189758b4aa6b83a24349a81c0a10ec1d25504e"},"q-0dc3e95ddbe2":{"correct":"B","answerText":"myocarditis","explanation":"Severe first-episode acute rheumatic carditis can impair myocardial function because of inflammatory myocarditis rather than longstanding valve stenosis.","optionReasons":{"B":"Severe first-episode acute rheumatic carditis can impair myocardial function because of inflammatory myocarditis rather than longstanding valve stenosis."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"06ed19afb699d42ca47735b81329446087000acedffd588c07aba65661729cda"},"q-eb858309c7dd":{"correct":"B","answerText":"mitral stenosis","explanation":"Mitral stenosis is the classic important residual valvular consequence of chronic rheumatic heart disease.","optionReasons":{"B":"Mitral stenosis is the classic important residual valvular consequence of chronic rheumatic heart disease."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"4e9c130baa8f4ba48afa8bc15dfdc409d68656e59e0ad97b5dbd3ce65f49fbdf"},"q-5effda082673":{"correct":"B","answerText":"emboli from valvular verrucae","explanation":"Rheumatic valve verrucae are usually small, sterile and firmly attached, making systemic embolization much less characteristic than in infective endocarditis.","optionReasons":{"B":"Rheumatic valve verrucae are usually small, sterile and firmly attached, making systemic embolization much less characteristic than in infective endocarditis."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"c365af5d1fd21551ec10f9f90486a0fc1cc590aa51a26e0abe7153e2678d2bbe"},"q-9e8239fb6774":{"correct":"E","answerText":"Aschoff body","explanation":"An Aschoff body is the characteristic histopathological lesion of active rheumatic carditis.","optionReasons":{"E":"An Aschoff body is the characteristic histopathological lesion of active rheumatic carditis."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"f2e8d1562b8489658bd8b7cc9543705080e69a1e5792f41f1bccd69f07f5ac5b"},"q-e7c8a5b82630":{"correct":"B","answerText":"dilatation and hypertrophy of the left ventricle","explanation":"Pure mitral stenosis causes elevated left atrial and pulmonary venous pressures; major left ventricular dilatation or hypertrophy is not characteristic.","optionReasons":{"B":"Pure mitral stenosis causes elevated left atrial and pulmonary venous pressures; major left ventricular dilatation or hypertrophy is not characteristic."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"540939ae8b6125bf8d6edf581cb8bdbf221aeea2c6bb9ec279f863af044f11f5"},"q-7d68b395257f":{"correct":"C","answerText":"frequently associated with mucin-producing adenocarcinomas","explanation":"Nonbacterial thrombotic endocarditis is associated with hypercoagulability and mucin-producing malignancies, especially adenocarcinoma.","optionReasons":{"C":"Nonbacterial thrombotic endocarditis is associated with hypercoagulability and mucin-producing malignancies, especially adenocarcinoma."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"d79bc105ff0bd36bf0d47be8136c878408d1a37df1e8a2f83384ea4596083a94"},"q-cec615995521":{"correct":"C","answerText":"left ventricular hypertrophy","explanation":"Mitral stenosis can cause atrial fibrillation, left atrial thrombus and pulmonary hypertension but usually not left ventricular hypertrophy.","optionReasons":{"C":"Mitral stenosis can cause atrial fibrillation, left atrial thrombus and pulmonary hypertension but usually not left ventricular hypertrophy."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"c84d607018c83e6990217433940c24c4a45dde0f9b33bac3a18170000ecd12b4"},"q-a29f3068baf1":{"correct":"B","answerText":"bicuspid aortic valve","explanation":"Congenital bicuspid aortic valves are prone to progressive calcific stenosis, often earlier in life than tricuspid valves.","optionReasons":{"B":"Congenital bicuspid aortic valves are prone to progressive calcific stenosis, often earlier in life than tricuspid valves."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"36a4c2a81fe71ab75ff9935f88b6151edfff9107b343c0ec8fa3961fa32df7c9"},"q-aa1e04ec4877":{"correct":"C","answerText":"rheumatic endocarditis","explanation":"Most acquired mitral stenosis is a late consequence of rheumatic valvulitis and commissural fusion.","optionReasons":{"C":"Most acquired mitral stenosis is a late consequence of rheumatic valvulitis and commissural fusion."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"eee494440576fb8b96a458ec33ce4d8603edc0db65f9c46189a150eecb29d5d5"},"q-d2557dad9750":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Staphylococcus aureus","explanation":"Staphylococcus aureus can produce aggressive destructive infective endocarditis with large friable vegetations and valve destruction.","optionReasons":{"D":"Staphylococcus aureus can produce aggressive destructive infective endocarditis with large friable vegetations and valve destruction."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"a6f649ba7222d26b86c217028e85fa9f9cf02f220f9fd7442c2b090c92cb12aa"},"q-dee783b59ff1":{"correct":"D","answerText":"rheumatic heart disease","explanation":"Rheumatic heart disease remains the archetypal cause of acquired mitral stenosis.","optionReasons":{"D":"Rheumatic heart disease remains the archetypal cause of acquired mitral stenosis."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"42420f684839065e953d24bcfbf8da6c1a8598f8999f1b8f7823026b0606ffbf"},"q-fd59470a367c":{"correct":"E","answerText":"all of the above","explanation":"Sterile or infective valve vegetations occur in rheumatic fever, lupus, bacterial endocarditis and nonbacterial thrombotic endocarditis.","optionReasons":{"E":"Sterile or infective valve vegetations occur in rheumatic fever, lupus, bacterial endocarditis and nonbacterial thrombotic endocarditis."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"b68feaaf81f84a11b8b356673744c8ba5edca30475b5898c4df7615f5463afed"},"q-597176dd829c":{"correct":"C","answerText":"lupus erythematosus","explanation":"Libman–Sacks endocarditis is associated with systemic lupus erythematosus and noninfective vegetations.","optionReasons":{"C":"Libman–Sacks endocarditis is associated with systemic lupus erythematosus and noninfective vegetations."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"fd6ad7c4c96881d1020c21595524212dba3f60cdacdea1662c249f4bda92af50"},"q-68772f58c120":{"correct":"B","answerText":"carcinoid tumor of ileum with metastases to liver","explanation":"Serotonin released by metastatic ileal carcinoid tumors can cause fibrous plaques of the right-sided cardiac valves.","optionReasons":{"B":"Serotonin released by metastatic ileal carcinoid tumors can cause fibrous plaques of the right-sided cardiac valves."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"23492a50f0744367db49b1b1f140293716536c46c2419b44fb7c5b9c2e4602c6"},"q-ef2f95193c45":{"correct":"A","answerText":"dilated","explanation":"Chronic heavy alcohol consumption can cause toxic dilated cardiomyopathy with ventricular dilatation and impaired systolic function.","optionReasons":{"A":"Chronic heavy alcohol consumption can cause toxic dilated cardiomyopathy with ventricular dilatation and impaired systolic function."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"8e0c4d22ebae7e23d28ce12e7809ef26d7868a187814b98ea74cda89301e9f01"},"q-0ec01036b791":{"correct":"E","answerText":"all of the above","explanation":"Myocarditis can follow viral infection or toxin exposure and may cause enzyme elevation and persistent myocardial fibrosis.","optionReasons":{"E":"Myocarditis can follow viral infection or toxin exposure and may cause enzyme elevation and persistent myocardial fibrosis."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"62880e7bbd21de40e38416a5a86607add6c609727c62e1d98386b7f8cc1b98f1"},"q-b10d78da4e03":{"correct":"B","answerText":"amyloidosis","explanation":"Cardiac amyloidosis causes interstitial deposition that restricts ventricular filling, producing restrictive cardiomyopathy.","optionReasons":{"B":"Cardiac amyloidosis causes interstitial deposition that restricts ventricular filling, producing restrictive cardiomyopathy."},"references":[],"review":"new_curated_independent_reasoning_without_external_verification","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"92a2c62682f07e01947d863e0b345048d66edc7aa5fcd144296fc0a3a5d8d7d3"},"q-9c6a15f3dfc7":{"correct":"E","answerText":"female reproductive","explanation":"Vitellaria produce yolk material and eggshell precursors in the female reproductive system of trematodes and cestodes.","optionReasons":{"E":"Vitellaria produce yolk material and eggshell precursors in the female reproductive system of trematodes and cestodes."},"references":[],"review":"exact_duplicate_of_new_independent_answer_oct20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"3adf76166a373a9e695a02342555364611430fb1e216185eaf4a944badea2bd0"},"q-946dda913396":{"correct":"B","answerText":"by eliminating the dog's exposure to fleas","explanation":"Dipylidium caninum infection follows ingestion of fleas containing cysticercoid larvae; effective flea control interrupts reinfection.","optionReasons":{"B":"Dipylidium caninum infection follows ingestion of fleas containing cysticercoid larvae; effective flea control interrupts reinfection."},"references":[],"review":"exact_duplicate_of_new_independent_answer_oct20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"0424b6e1c2214b3555561403d436de52cfec66d50944aed09c384c37eb5241c1"},"q-1655dfc724b2":{"correct":"B","answerText":"miracidium","explanation":"The ciliated miracidium hatches from the trematode egg and actively penetrates a suitable snail intermediate host.","optionReasons":{"B":"The ciliated miracidium hatches from the trematode egg and actively penetrates a suitable snail intermediate host."},"references":[],"review":"exact_duplicate_of_new_independent_answer_oct20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"5bdef88ed58ed233437afaa54d08cb29552abcd4b32cd02b62393d26266b12af"},"q-c7fa255db737":{"correct":"D","answerText":"accidental ingestion of eggs excreted in feces","explanation":"Echinococcus multilocularis infects intermediate hosts when parasite eggs shed by infected canids are ingested.","optionReasons":{"D":"Echinococcus multilocularis infects intermediate hosts when parasite eggs shed by infected canids are ingested."},"references":[],"review":"exact_duplicate_of_new_independent_answer_oct20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"0a1ada3256b80ed085b1d2c60a66b87a4f90346006feeb03aa589b5d08e65dd5"},"q-04be02e8a0d7":{"correct":"D","answerText":"accidental ingestion of eggs excreted in feces","explanation":"Echinococcus multilocularis infects intermediate hosts when parasite eggs shed by infected canids are ingested.","optionReasons":{"D":"Echinococcus multilocularis infects intermediate hosts when parasite eggs shed by infected canids are ingested."},"references":[],"review":"exact_duplicate_of_new_independent_answer_o