esthetic, so low potency is the incorrect description.","optionReasons":{"B":"Tetracaine is a potent, relatively long-acting ester local anesthetic, so low potency is the incorrect description."},"references":[],"review":"exact_duplicate_of_new_independent_answer_oct20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"c347fb6fa434f8566b743890d6a0004f25648ac6d8736961dfcc7035c14fa0c9"},"q-f0cd1835882d":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Neostigmine","explanation":"Neostigmine inhibits acetylcholinesterase and also has direct nicotinic agonist activity at the neuromuscular junction.","optionReasons":{"C":"Neostigmine inhibits acetylcholinesterase and also has direct nicotinic agonist activity at the neuromuscular junction."},"references":[],"review":"exact_duplicate_of_new_independent_answer_oct20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"43690e3beb8657bd785b55372397ee174c18d0f65985bfb4469fb318c4af0192"},"q-c36576a832d3":{"correct":"A","answerText":"The salivary, bronchial and sweat glands","explanation":"Salivary, bronchial and sweat secretions are particularly sensitive to antimuscarinic inhibition.","optionReasons":{"A":"Salivary, bronchial and sweat secretions are particularly sensitive to antimuscarinic inhibition."},"references":[],"review":"exact_duplicate_of_new_independent_answer_oct20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"736e1c58c908bd4bc4bec62a54a6ac56800f7c73ab3e236d0566d50af45813d3"},"q-4dc59b59fa49":{"correct":"C","answerText":"In infants and children","explanation":"Young children have a higher risk of antimuscarinic hyperthermia because sweating is inhibited, impairing heat loss.","optionReasons":{"C":"Young children have a higher risk of antimuscarinic hyperthermia because sweating is inhibited, impairing heat loss."},"references":[],"review":"exact_duplicate_of_new_independent_answer_oct20","reviewDate":"20