answerText":"50:1","explanation":"Lowering pH by one unit increases the weak-acid-to-conjugate-base ratio tenfold; 5:1 becomes 50:1 by the Henderson–Hasselbalch relationship.","optionReasons":{"C":"Lowering pH by one unit increases the weak-acid-to-conjugate-base ratio tenfold; 5:1 becomes 50:1 by the Henderson–Hasselbalch relationship."},"references":[],"review":"exact_duplicate_of_new_independent_answer_oct20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"6c8bfacac3f7ad520dda46df751eb8e37a688c082e24e32b72ec6be25fe2d9a6"},"q-45e4529161c1":{"correct":"A","answerText":"the posterior pituitary to release more ADH","explanation":"Raised plasma osmolality stimulates hypothalamic osmoreceptors, increasing posterior-pituitary vasopressin (ADH) release to conserve water.","optionReasons":{"A":"Raised plasma osmolality stimulates hypothalamic osmoreceptors, increasing posterior-pituitary vasopressin (ADH) release to conserve water."},"references":[],"review":"exact_duplicate_of_new_independent_answer_oct20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"719c294ec9602bc74d95f722d6b5cbbe0f683e69a845ba9cd64f3aaf68c8f152"},"q-5519056a3fb4":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Cyclooxygenase","explanation":"Cyclooxygenase enzymes convert arachidonic acid into prostaglandin precursors; lipoxygenase instead generates leukotrienes and related lipid mediators.","optionReasons":{"A":"Cyclooxygenase enzymes convert arachidonic acid into prostaglandin precursors; lipoxygenase instead generates leukotrienes and related lipid mediators."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"68cddeafbb409bed82c8fb11cad13a917a3e5a78f705ede1060a52ae43ebb8b7"},"q-6fd63d68c226":{"correct":"E","answerText":"Neutrophils","explanation":"Neutrophil lysosomal hydrolases are major contributors to liquefactive tissue breakdown and pus formation in an abscess.","optionReasons":{"E":"Neutrophil lysosomal hydrolases are major contributors to liquefactive tissue breakdown and pus formation in an abscess."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"73e0b932ea0c4cdeb06efd4b714ae3f636dad1d6ffb1a21c12cd2b8aec4d98bc"},"q-0850558260eb":{"correct":"C","answerText":"inhibition of certain enzymes which break down some drugs.","explanation":"Cimetidine and erythromycin can inhibit hepatic drug-metabolizing enzymes, slowing the breakdown of susceptible coadministered drugs and increasing their exposure.","optionReasons":{"C":"Cimetidine and erythromycin can inhibit hepatic drug-metabolizing enzymes, slowing the breakdown of susceptible coadministered drugs and increasing their exposure."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"f343a87126585026b01da897e9c561df7ad32c1f2b077c52103aa22dc57c6a93"},"q-cda330b1f9d7":{"correct":"E","answerText":"it is usually occurs due to enzyme induction or inhibition.","explanation":"Presystemic (first-pass) metabolism occurs before drug reaches the systemic circulation, typically in intestinal mucosa and liver. It is not defined by, nor does it usually occur because of, enzyme induction or inhibition.","optionReasons":{"E":"Presystemic (first-pass) metabolism occurs before drug reaches the systemic circulation, typically in intestinal mucosa and liver. It is not defined by, nor does it usually occur because of, enzyme induction or inhibition."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"2397a9991fe5167e9aae65aa6c72d6ffd0eee313a994e89cbf7290238767e103"},"q-2822b38f1ffa":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Increased enzyme synthesis rates and metabolism for certain drugs","explanation":"Induction of certain cytochrome P450 enzymes increases the amount of active enzyme and commonly speeds metabolism of substrate drugs; it does not directly increase their protein binding.","optionReasons":{"A":"Induction of certain cytochrome P450 enzymes increases the amount of active enzyme and commonly speeds metabolism of substrate drugs; it does not directly increase their protein binding."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"fa71a657faa3e12aeedd2f14d9c0179267f3a881fec8c29413405b7aab21b823"},"q-a14a3f26a944":{"correct":"E","answerText":"protonation","explanation":"In acidic solution, a weak acid is more protonated and unionized, usually increasing lipid solubility and reducing water solubility. The relevant acid-base process is protonation.","optionReasons":{"E":"In acidic solution, a weak acid is more protonated and unionized, usually increasing lipid solubility and reducing water solubility. The relevant acid-base process is protonation."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"cfbf53dc04c9c857ff4d4b7cdf27c4fa93b5e7e09696befc6dfd538455541f22"},"q-e754043659d1":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Microsomal enzymes","explanation":"The microsomal cytochrome P450 system is a classic inducible drug-metabolizing enzyme system, notably in the hepatic smooth endoplasmic reticulum.","optionReasons":{"A":"The microsomal cytochrome P450 system is a classic inducible drug-metabolizing enzyme system, notably in the hepatic smooth endoplasmic reticulum."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"133ffff4f1de42706580f23ebe4d002adb00c73a53febdea25d3538a614203ee"},"q-cfcd23010ffe":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Increased synthesis of enzyme protein (p. 24)","explanation":"Enzyme induction generally reflects increased synthesis of metabolizing enzyme protein, unlike immediate competitive inhibition or a change in substrate transport.","optionReasons":{"D":"Enzyme induction generally reflects increased synthesis of metabolizing enzyme protein, unlike immediate competitive inhibition or a change in substrate transport."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"c2601d2f25c0f30ddc9e9c8ffafe47d492254507c05f66524705c80739f6815b"},"q-803420860017":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Takes about one week to develop","explanation":"Classic microsomal enzyme induction develops over days and may take approximately a week to become established; it is reversible and cannot treat most acute toxic exposures quickly.","optionReasons":{"A":"Classic microsomal enzyme induction develops over days and may take approximately a week to become established; it is reversible and cannot treat most acute toxic exposures quickly."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"90c756cce48abf3dafd9a7845364ca52e72882cb77fe53630797237994ae9ab4"},"q-9c2bc55666ed":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Edrophonium","explanation":"Edrophonium binds reversibly to the anionic site of acetylcholinesterase through noncovalent interactions; carbamate agents modify the esteratic site.","optionReasons":{"C":"Edrophonium binds reversibly to the anionic site of acetylcholinesterase through noncovalent interactions; carbamate agents modify the esteratic site."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"1b72333a22521eeb0d580d182fd4a372610859013e8d3876b257a97af23087d1"},"q-98418e39407a":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Organophosphate anticholinesterases","explanation":"Pralidoxime can reactivate acetylcholinesterase inhibited by organophosphates before enzyme aging, by removing the phosphate group. This is not the usual management of carbamate inhibition.","optionReasons":{"B":"Pralidoxime can reactivate acetylcholinesterase inhibited by organophosphates before enzyme aging, by removing the phosphate group. This is not the usual management of carbamate inhibition."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"027b198332f7be786c5cb2fa8f430809d083bff57482d404c39c1de407e0c794"},"q-51b81f67a0d6":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Tyrosine hydroxylase","explanation":"Tyrosine hydroxylase catalyzes the rate-limiting conversion of tyrosine to DOPA during catecholamine biosynthesis.","optionReasons":{"A":"Tyrosine hydroxylase catalyzes the rate-limiting conversion of tyrosine to DOPA during catecholamine biosynthesis."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"6aa6bf20f89a8af7469abd66f8467df23ffb00bcdfc5cc8fbf0f47f6b4512872"},"q-ea39ecc59814":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Inhibition of neoglucogenesis in liver","explanation":"Adrenaline promotes rather than inhibits hepatic gluconeogenesis through adrenergic signaling; its metabolic actions also include glycogenolysis and lipolysis.","optionReasons":{"B":"Adrenaline promotes rather than inhibits hepatic gluconeogenesis through adrenergic signaling; its metabolic actions also include glycogenolysis and lipolysis."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"2f89ec55941e4c04dfc0ac078e928505f4b05d5bdde9f7f3089b925b722d82ab"},"q-6f7c5321a5b0":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Induction ceases within a few days of withdrawal of drug","explanation":"The effects of enzyme induction may persist longer than just a few days after stopping an inducer because induced enzyme protein must turn over.","optionReasons":{"C":"The effects of enzyme induction may persist longer than just a few days after stopping an inducer because induced enzyme protein must turn over."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"3b0e4d7ac540554c64f8a8c7d2ff621d325531432436274be5e56aa0ca78e901"},"q-efe1446d1b85":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Chloramphenicol","explanation":"Chloramphenicol inhibits microsomal drug-metabolizing enzymes rather than inducing them; phenytoin and cigarette-smoke constituents are well-known enzyme inducers.","optionReasons":{"D":"Chloramphenicol inhibits microsomal drug-metabolizing enzymes rather than inducing them; phenytoin and cigarette-smoke constituents are well-known enzyme inducers."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"367a3497082d7f2f4512f21215e0c74cb26697781bee16b2b2f28f682dbdc76e"},"q-3d271dc783de":{"correct":"B","answerText":"It is inducible","explanation":"COX-2 is an inducible cyclooxygenase expressed in response to inflammatory stimuli, unlike the generally constitutive COX-1 enzyme.","optionReasons":{"B":"COX-2 is an inducible cyclooxygenase expressed in response to inflammatory stimuli, unlike the generally constitutive COX-1 enzyme."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"2611c9cd39b0c5e87430da74faebab3708756e7ac182e013448eb1a588f26157"},"q-7e70aa432d27":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Keep the eyelids from sticking together","explanation":"Meibomian glands produce the lipid component of the tear film, which lubricates the lid margins and reduces adhesion between the eyelids.","optionReasons":{"D":"Meibomian glands produce the lipid component of the tear film, which lubricates the lid margins and reduces adhesion between the eyelids."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"cbb37323f1639d1d73b5d9310f354c7401256c3c496318d701cc550f4692b52e"},"q-8b0ac89a979c":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Glycolysis.","explanation":"Glycolysis is a linked sequence of enzyme-catalyzed chemical reactions; ATP and oxaloacetate are individual molecules, not pathways.","optionReasons":{"C":"Glycolysis is a linked sequence of enzyme-catalyzed chemical reactions; ATP and oxaloacetate are individual molecules, not pathways."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"603307c15974339c36bdbecf45294031c0e530a92a7cc9777463caf8e0875c3e"},"q-491943da8850":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Cimetidine","explanation":"Cimetidine is the H2 blocker classically associated with substantial inhibition of several hepatic cytochrome P450 enzymes, unlike the newer H2 blockers listed.","optionReasons":{"A":"Cimetidine is the H2 blocker classically associated with substantial inhibition of several hepatic cytochrome P450 enzymes, unlike the newer H2 blockers listed."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"b654a3cd1a892b66f4f319c278ceeeaa1e9f3ed48fdea70971e21e7e1ad68124"},"q-c8ca7a77e862":{"correct":"A","answerText":"the pH of a buffer does not change on addition of acid or base.","explanation":"Buffers resist large changes in pH but do not prevent all change when acid or base is added. The claim that pH does not change is therefore incorrect.","optionReasons":{"A":"Buffers resist large changes in pH but do not prevent all change when acid or base is added. The claim that pH does not change is therefore incorrect."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"00c261c71e2e2e20cdb4cba28c496e02203c059ecffe7c0a06f8800771d14320"},"q-a4e0cfa3af99":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Reduces concentration of angiotensin II","explanation":"ACE inhibition reduces formation of angiotensin II and reduces aldosterone stimulation while increasing, not decreasing, bradykinin by preventing its breakdown.","optionReasons":{"A":"ACE inhibition reduces formation of angiotensin II and reduces aldosterone stimulation while increasing, not decreasing, bradykinin by preventing its breakdown."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"3ae3bc9a16a863ae46ca4351d728c47e6a7d28f0a4227dfbde97208dcf8cf0bc"},"q-8dbde2681737":{"correct":"E","answerText":"Pectineus is a lateral relation.","explanation":"Pectineus lies anterior and medial to the hip joint and is not properly described as its lateral relation.","optionReasons":{"E":"Pectineus lies anterior and medial to the hip joint and is not properly described as its lateral relation."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"df9fa72dc437fcd5ca14ff80bc79d6dbdec962abcd11b3af1cdd154274995d3b"},"q-2475960bc088":{"correct":"B","answerText":"The artery to the head of the femur is a branch of the femoral artery.","explanation":"The small artery in the ligament of the femoral head usually arises from the obturator artery, not directly from the femoral artery as stated.","optionReasons":{"B":"The small artery in the ligament of the femoral head usually arises from the obturator artery, not directly from the femoral artery as stated."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"e90f397fc569a9ce5c940c8909d2f21ccd414b33cd9233d1d210e2ba07f89ac1"},"q-865d0ae74f56":{"correct":"D","answerText":"It contributes to the blood supply of the breast.","explanation":"The internal thoracic artery gives perforating and anterior intercostal branches that contribute to vascular supply of the breast.","optionReasons":{"D":"The internal thoracic artery gives perforating and anterior intercostal branches that contribute to vascular supply of the breast."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"58a5cd2e3a7b140fea8ecb9a4bcee62a624cf03c62b67e24a541a3654ab23d88"},"q-ffc5969901da":{"correct":"B","answerText":"The inferior mediastinum is conventionally divided into three parts.","explanation":"The inferior mediastinum is conventionally divided into anterior, middle, and posterior compartments below the transverse thoracic plane.","optionReasons":{"B":"The inferior mediastinum is conventionally divided into anterior, middle, and posterior compartments below the transverse thoracic plane."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"5830ea3b294e6d4b1d92e808de494a0a982b036ff0c5ef890c1646d6e930bf40"},"q-10e137a06045":{"correct":"D","answerText":"It is lined by mucus secreting cells.","explanation":"The trachea is lined predominantly by respiratory epithelium with mucus-producing goblet cells that support mucociliary clearance.","optionReasons":{"D":"The trachea is lined predominantly by respiratory epithelium with mucus-producing goblet cells that support mucociliary clearance."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"95f93d8548a6292dd3891aad12a685cdc7171603ea70368ffa9b362c79ba0d65"},"q-d3ba0fdb081e":{"correct":"B","answerText":"The azygos vein drains into its posterior aspect.","explanation":"The azygos vein forms an arch over the right lung root and enters the posterior aspect of the superior vena cava.","optionReasons":{"B":"The azygos vein forms an arch over the right lung root and enters the posterior aspect of the superior vena cava."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"1b9ecf76914ce4d1ac0ca6e4d754bc06636d83f5bed83e10c8bdde40cce87c39"},"q-7ed15af42bc5":{"correct":"B","answerText":"The opening of the inferior vena cava into the right atrium is valveless.","explanation":"The inferior vena caval opening into the right atrium may have a remnant Eustachian valve, so calling the opening entirely valveless is incorrect.","optionReasons":{"B":"The inferior vena caval opening into the right atrium may have a remnant Eustachian valve, so calling the opening entirely valveless is incorrect."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"ace5885b52cbc33f8f9a0ff55fa95e17aaec92f75d8fcc0d7fd5a4330fb9eb97"},"q-52c84094ad32":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Its wall has a smooth and a rough portion.","explanation":"The left ventricle has a smooth-walled outflow tract (aortic vestibule) and a trabeculated inflow region.","optionReasons":{"D":"The left ventricle has a smooth-walled outflow tract (aortic vestibule) and a trabeculated inflow region."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"3b055ff0aff26fb09420fcfa29bc068b966d3bca7f1872814abf71fda35f1485"},"q-b1c65b1df915":{"correct":"E","answerText":"It empties into the left subclavian artery. 57","explanation":"The thoracic duct normally terminates at or near the left venous angle formed by the internal jugular and subclavian veins, not in the subclavian artery.","optionReasons":{"E":"The thoracic duct normally terminates at or near the left venous angle formed by the internal jugular and subclavian veins, not in the subclavian artery."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"d628df8d88af9ddbf8b66d214a6599982cdf160d8a79451b22566ea8bc5c7f82"},"q-4320955f49d1":{"correct":"C","answerText":"The aorta usually gives rise to the majority of the posterior intercostal arteries.","explanation":"The descending thoracic aorta provides most posterior intercostal arteries; the first two spaces usually receive arteries via the supreme intercostal branch.","optionReasons":{"C":"The descending thoracic aorta provides most posterior intercostal arteries; the first two spaces usually receive arteries via the supreme intercostal branch."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"8d9c41b4f926235017387ecc3ddf90d67292f28ae6c47b1cc5403fe6c122ee40"},"q-3b658228116e":{"correct":"E","answerText":"Its fibres pass to the oesophagus to form the oesophageal plexus. 58","explanation":"Fibers from the vagus contribute to the esophageal plexus, from which vagal trunks form before traversing the diaphragm.","optionReasons":{"E":"Fibers from the vagus contribute to the esophageal plexus, from which vagal trunks form before traversing the diaphragm."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"27cf11df8891afb16807c357becaa0e8830c56b8147a814b54be06f6e13267a9"},"q-119d9a5c6ec0":{"correct":"A","answerText":"It is attached to the xiphoid.","explanation":"The diaphragm has a sternal attachment from the posterior surface of the xiphoid process. The esophageal opening is at T10 and Bochdalek defects are posterolateral.","optionReasons":{"A":"The diaphragm has a sternal attachment from the posterior surface of the xiphoid process. The esophageal opening is at T10 and Bochdalek defects are posterolateral."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"70860f74a402df5d95a007d60157127066199dd3707c3e9917dd0b03dd04d4ca"},"q-6f803bfbcecf":{"correct":"E","answerText":"The common bile duct is contained within the anterior border.","explanation":"The anterior boundary of the epiploic foramen is the hepatoduodenal ligament, containing the common bile duct, portal vein, and proper hepatic artery.","optionReasons":{"E":"The anterior boundary of the epiploic foramen is the hepatoduodenal ligament, containing the common bile duct, portal vein, and proper hepatic artery."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"dd8ebf895caa496937631badfc6f6bf614a9f7d995fe8fd75c4ae36ed0c22f4e"},"q-c287fb36aebe":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Sexual reproduction occurs","explanation":"A definitive host is the host in which a parasite reaches sexual maturity or undergoes sexual reproduction; asexual stages often occur in intermediate hosts.","optionReasons":{"C":"A definitive host is the host in which a parasite reaches sexual maturity or undergoes sexual reproduction; asexual stages often occur in intermediate hosts."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"f5f67a8fca870d9c903227f987874becf42582b48c2356e0ba12ce877d91cde3"},"q-015c2fec39e6":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Ookinete","explanation":"The ookinete is the motile stage formed after gamete fusion that penetrates the mosquito midgut wall before developing into an oocyst.","optionReasons":{"B":"The ookinete is the motile stage formed after gamete fusion that penetrates the mosquito midgut wall before developing into an oocyst."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"de689ac8c3bee18f6f9c4ba3eb10517f7896b3adc0d77c1d2fb12a8e4d5066a9"},"q-954ff0eae335":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Epimastigote","explanation":"Trypanosoma cruzi multiplies in the triatomine insect midgut as the epimastigote stage before developing into infective metacyclic trypomastigotes.","optionReasons":{"B":"Trypanosoma cruzi multiplies in the triatomine insect midgut as the epimastigote stage before developing into infective metacyclic trypomastigotes."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"fdf68725658de11b880047d12b6bd6f2bc138f01d06f5ec3a19df7f4f8434e12"},"q-a21308b8fbbd":{"correct":"A","answerText":"First trimester","explanation":"Congenital toxoplasmosis is generally most severe when primary maternal infection occurs early in pregnancy, although transmission probability increases later in gestation.","optionReasons":{"A":"Congenital toxoplasmosis is generally most severe when primary maternal infection occurs early in pregnancy, although transmission probability increases later in gestation."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"b4e6106725759189bc0d3d4c664368cb5bfbdee630ac8154ffe64454efa6f6e0"},"q-0c39b813888c":{"correct":"B","answerText":"The ability to kill cells in contact dependent manner","explanation":"Entamoeba histolytica trophozoites adhere to and lyse host cells through contact-dependent cytotoxic mechanisms that contribute to tissue invasion.","optionReasons":{"B":"Entamoeba histolytica trophozoites adhere to and lyse host cells through contact-dependent cytotoxic mechanisms that contribute to tissue invasion."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"c4ef6005cb5b2644fa25b260f024a21b5bb7d49e72a88b7a2ab09dbcc7cde292"},"q-c620f85d85fb":{"correct":"C","answerText":"tetrathyridian","explanation":"The tetrathyridium larval stage of certain cestodes can transfer between successive paratenic hosts while remaining infective.","optionReasons":{"C":"The tetrathyridium larval stage of certain cestodes can transfer between successive paratenic hosts while remaining infective."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"9d9830ef78d8af578cc6acf25e2399768e9ccf1538142f638be8bdd9b04bc44c"},"q-7417d959697b":{"correct":"E","answerText":"All of the above","explanation":"Parasites may enter hosts through ingestion, bites from vectors, direct skin penetration, or sexual contact; all the listed routes are recognized modes of parasite acquisition.","optionReasons":{"E":"Parasites may enter hosts through ingestion, bites from vectors, direct skin penetration, or sexual contact; all the listed routes are recognized modes of parasite acquisition."},"references":[],"review":"independent_provisional_reasoning_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"d7e49c673d60a335e68209f9f33061728800507ec527bfae5d4a65f665242d48"},"q-29c7fe97a6dd":{"correct":"C","answerText":"tetrathyridian","explanation":"The tetrathyridium larval stage of certain cestodes can transfer between successive paratenic hosts while remaining infective.","optionReasons":{"C":"The tetrathyridium larval stage of certain cestodes can transfer between successive paratenic hosts while remaining infective."},"references":[],"review":"exact_duplicate_of_new_independent_reasoning","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"questionTextHash":"9d9830ef78d8af578cc6acf25e2399768e9ccf1538142f638be8bdd9b04bc44c"},"q-0f6f20459bab":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Microsomal oxidation results in an increase of ionization and water solubility of a drug","explanation":"Phase I microsomal oxidation usually introduces or exposes polar groups, making a drug or metabolite more water soluble. Oxidation can also activate prodrugs or form toxic metabolites, so it is not invariably detoxifying.","optionReasons":{"C":"Phase I microsomal oxidation usually introduces or exposes polar groups, making a drug or metabolite more water soluble. Oxidation can also activate prodrugs or form toxic metabolites, so it is not invariably detoxifying."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"c452514625a06b2666a08aa19de0586e9bc0927a4f6dc6ed3be9df8e7ec639e1"},"q-b5bb93d10e15":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Coupling of a drug with an endogenous substrate","explanation":"Drug conjugation is a phase II reaction in which the drug or its metabolite is linked to an endogenous moiety such as glucuronic acid, sulfate or glutathione.","optionReasons":{"C":"Drug conjugation is a phase II reaction in which the drug or its metabolite is linked to an endogenous moiety such as glucuronic acid, sulfate or glutathione."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"cacd11b80b265f1989df5fddda8f71a45267c75e4efe7e6f1dd8816b432ae617"},"q-40b111ae73bb":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Active macromolecular components of a cell or an organism which a drug molecule has to combine with in order to elicit its specific effect","explanation":"A receptor is a macromolecular target whose interaction with a ligand initiates or modifies a biological response; it need not be limited to an ion channel or an enzyme.","optionReasons":{"C":"A receptor is a macromolecular target whose interaction with a ligand initiates or modifies a biological response; it need not be limited to an ion channel or an enzyme."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"4fab59b5282bcb2197f431e28f874a589c7d6347c1412ef7168c5176f24621ff"},"q-9727f1a2cfe1":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Gene replacement by the introduction of a therapeutic gene to correct a genetic effect","explanation":"Gene replacement therapy is a genetic intervention, not a conventional membrane-receptor signal-transduction mechanism. Ligand-gated channels, receptor kinases and G-protein-coupled receptors all transmit signals.","optionReasons":{"B":"Gene replacement therapy is a genetic intervention, not a conventional membrane-receptor signal-transduction mechanism. Ligand-gated channels, receptor kinases and G-protein-coupled receptors all transmit signals."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"dc5aa6cffbd45ebfd291c8c2e487f2244e0376b29b0ae462f2ecf1c5ef5279bb"},"q-0722d239a361":{"correct":"D","answerText":"The ED50 is a measure of drug’s efficacy","explanation":"ED50 is the dose producing a specified effect in 50 percent of a population, or 50 percent maximal effect in a graded-response setting; it measures potency, not maximal efficacy.","optionReasons":{"D":"ED50 is the dose producing a specified effect in 50 percent of a population, or 50 percent maximal effect in a graded-response setting; it measures potency, not maximal efficacy."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"ee669992e955855d930d1afca205789dcbda790b8aa404a10f442dce4c67b7ac"},"q-11d62b8986c1":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Very rapidly developing tolerance","explanation":"Tachyphylaxis refers to rapidly developing tolerance over repeated doses given close together; ordinary tolerance often develops more gradually.","optionReasons":{"B":"Tachyphylaxis refers to rapidly developing tolerance over repeated doses given close together; ordinary tolerance often develops more gradually."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"a106af92d50136c421aa5983459f784177cd0af1ea1294aedd2501555a0c23f8"},"q-1ad596ff7169":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Synergism","explanation":"Synergism is a drug interaction in which combined activity exceeds what would be expected from the individual effects; tolerance and accumulation do not specifically require two drugs.","optionReasons":{"D":"Synergism is a drug interaction in which combined activity exceeds what would be expected from the individual effects; tolerance and accumulation do not specifically require two drugs."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"7f4607b8a28c9dde0e9626db5488fb47ada80e51420d46768b139076288625c4"},"q-d36e5d4ff63b":{"correct":"A","answerText":"A ratio used to evaluate the safety and usefulness of a drug for indication","explanation":"The therapeutic index compares doses associated with toxic and therapeutic effects (classically TD50/ED50), serving as a rough measure of relative drug safety.","optionReasons":{"A":"The therapeutic index compares doses associated with toxic and therapeutic effects (classically TD50/ED50), serving as a rough measure of relative drug safety."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"da3181b1c23f0b67a0c632dbe2d87ae067534e05717428736c3593ebdb940d95"},"q-8d8f4df03a0c":{"correct":"B","answerText":"B and C fibers","explanation":"Small autonomic B fibers and many small-diameter C fibers are particularly susceptible to local anesthetic blockade; large myelinated motor A-alpha fibers generally require greater exposure.","optionReasons":{"B":"Small autonomic B fibers and many small-diameter C fibers are particularly susceptible to local anesthetic blockade; large myelinated motor A-alpha fibers generally require greater exposure."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"c37a8b981dabcec56b9ae4a1b5d9133fd0cf671f80e0ec203c1579d536c122df"},"q-ac359b42504e":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Neostigmine","explanation":"Neostigmine inhibits acetylcholinesterase, increasing acetylcholine at the neuromuscular junction and improving transmission in myasthenia gravis. Edrophonium is too short acting for routine maintenance therapy.","optionReasons":{"B":"Neostigmine inhibits acetylcholinesterase, increasing acetylcholine at the neuromuscular junction and improving transmission in myasthenia gravis. Edrophonium is too short acting for routine maintenance therapy."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"d8551f937fc5e86a16aa8d7aaa59483cd6bdbccfeeacf635e02efc48bc901094"},"q-cdd0b8e71272":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Physostigmine","explanation":"Physostigmine is a tertiary acetylcholinesterase inhibitor that enters the CNS and can reverse serious central as well as peripheral antimuscarinic toxicity under monitored conditions.","optionReasons":{"C":"Physostigmine is a tertiary acetylcholinesterase inhibitor that enters the CNS and can reverse serious central as well as peripheral antimuscarinic toxicity under monitored conditions."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"3fabda8ebaf26dd0010bd9bad94f8537ffb785107b86bb67689408a9fe105b51"},"q-8fcb6a95b518":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Weakness of all skeletal muscles","explanation":"Excess muscarinic stimulation causes salivation, bronchorrhea, bradycardia, miosis, intestinal cramping and diarrhea; skeletal muscle weakness is caused predominantly by nicotinic neuromuscular effects.","optionReasons":{"D":"Excess muscarinic stimulation causes salivation, bronchorrhea, bradycardia, miosis, intestinal cramping and diarrhea; skeletal muscle weakness is caused predominantly by nicotinic neuromuscular effects."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"7510205821506bd672895f1dccdbbac53503ee8ecf62399b243df5bb0705e2d6"},"q-26dc2308e400":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Atropine","explanation":"Atropine competitively antagonizes muscarinic acetylcholine receptors and thereby blocks the muscarinic effects of pilocarpine and choline esters.","optionReasons":{"B":"Atropine competitively antagonizes muscarinic acetylcholine receptors and thereby blocks the muscarinic effects of pilocarpine and choline esters."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"6317e0bec265189c0c6f1694398e1f309af4887c4a047e219631376a46b72663"},"q-67bbf979924a":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Mydriasis","explanation":"Organophosphate and other cholinesterase-inhibitor poisoning causes cholinergic miosis rather than mydriasis, alongside sweating, secretions, bronchospasm and gastrointestinal hypermotility.","optionReasons":{"B":"Organophosphate and other cholinesterase-inhibitor poisoning causes cholinergic miosis rather than mydriasis, alongside sweating, secretions, bronchospasm and gastrointestinal hypermotility."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"bca3deffbd9d68a0474a2a7f343ff391bee39489e1f10db17a8764730dcdd747"},"q-cdbcf337ce87":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Mydriasis, a rise in intraocular pressure and cycloplegia","explanation":"Atropine blocks parasympathetic muscarinic control of the iris sphincter and ciliary muscle, producing mydriasis and cycloplegia; pressure can rise in susceptible eyes.","optionReasons":{"B":"Atropine blocks parasympathetic muscarinic control of the iris sphincter and ciliary muscle, producing mydriasis and cycloplegia; pressure can rise in susceptible eyes."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"0b6c5823253dcbb8600a90a94dd3acd958fc4479bee439c967f78226523c2d5d"},"q-7a88c243571a":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Tachycardia, little effect on blood pressure and bronchodilation","explanation":"Atropine inhibits cardiac vagal signaling and bronchial smooth-muscle muscarinic receptors, commonly increasing heart rate and promoting bronchodilation with little direct effect on arterial pressure.","optionReasons":{"B":"Atropine inhibits cardiac vagal signaling and bronchial smooth-muscle muscarinic receptors, commonly increasing heart rate and promoting bronchodilation with little direct effect on arterial pressure."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"ac3ee488da8ffb91fae18054c9ea53d6eda48f6e74a69d7aa0005326e633a1c1"},"q-c969e0ea97ac":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Spasmolitic activity","explanation":"Atropine decreases gastrointestinal smooth-muscle tone and motility through muscarinic receptor antagonism, yielding antispasmodic effects rather than increased secretion or contraction.","optionReasons":{"A":"Atropine decreases gastrointestinal smooth-muscle tone and motility through muscarinic receptor antagonism, yielding antispasmodic effects rather than increased secretion or contraction."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"be7f745c6fb5a88d80e89fec8758cd90a36da0cfe30f069623b686120c2a612d"},"q-aec54ab02e3c":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Interaction with adrenoreceptors","explanation":"Direct receptor agonism is a direct sympathomimetic mechanism; indirect action instead increases endogenous catecholamine availability by facilitating release or inhibiting uptake or metabolism.","optionReasons":{"C":"Direct receptor agonism is a direct sympathomimetic mechanism; indirect action instead increases endogenous catecholamine availability by facilitating release or inhibiting uptake or metabolism."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"1ea23774379514c7785c77eccbdbbf8888868d509803504e8caed6ecd952f903"},"q-9c03fac30261":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Ephedrine","explanation":"Ephedrine is not a catecholamine because it lacks the catechol ring; epinephrine, norepinephrine and isoproterenol have catechol structures.","optionReasons":{"A":"Ephedrine is not a catecholamine because it lacks the catechol ring; epinephrine, norepinephrine and isoproterenol have catechol structures."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"3b86ff8103309d083be3761858fc7afcc071f57d0abfefd293e97d5e12167b09"},"q-4b1fa78f8861":{"correct":"B","answerText":"α2 receptor","explanation":"The alpha-2 adrenoceptor couples to inhibitory Gi proteins and reduces adenylyl cyclase activity, lowering cellular cyclic AMP.","optionReasons":{"B":"The alpha-2 adrenoceptor couples to inhibitory Gi proteins and reduces adenylyl cyclase activity, lowering cellular cyclic AMP."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"8f82ec7d3115de8a126eefc0e425d08d43940117563c12fc2584682fa5f9eab6"},"q-7db1b7824e1a":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Skeletal muscle vessels have predominantly alfa receptors and constrict in the presence of epinephrine and norepinephrine","explanation":"Skeletal-muscle vessels have important beta-2-mediated vasodilator responses to circulating epinephrine, so they cannot be described as exclusively alpha-constricting vessels.","optionReasons":{"D":"Skeletal-muscle vessels have important beta-2-mediated vasodilator responses to circulating epinephrine, so they cannot be described as exclusively alpha-constricting vessels."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"f10ad76682ad257417fd921a2f8efc2cba9ff1efc2d0cc3df14b8a82e2784ded"},"q-607fad419be8":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Tachycardia","explanation":"Direct beta-1 receptor stimulation in the heart raises sinus-node firing and contractility, producing tachycardia rather than bronchodilation or reflex bradycardia.","optionReasons":{"C":"Direct beta-1 receptor stimulation in the heart raises sinus-node firing and contractility, producing tachycardia rather than bronchodilation or reflex bradycardia."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"e155c1f43501819088b83588380caf19c11e844839e174be6d5057a5c22c895e"},"q-36e54024442e":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Pupillary dilator muscle","explanation":"The radial dilator of the pupil uses alpha-1 receptors, whereas beta receptors are prominent in myocardium, bronchial smooth muscle and adipose tissue.","optionReasons":{"C":"The radial dilator of the pupil uses alpha-1 receptors, whereas beta receptors are prominent in myocardium, bronchial smooth muscle and adipose tissue."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"7c1da478906e9d6033dbbdd6fd5a2b291c8e9df957c1ab3281790cfcf26baff9"},"q-5291eba50263":{"correct":"D","answerText":"All of the above","explanation":"Sympathomimetics can alter blood pressure by changing cardiac output, systemic vascular resistance and venous capacitance/return; the overall response reflects all three contributions.","optionReasons":{"D":"Sympathomimetics can alter blood pressure by changing cardiac output, systemic vascular resistance and venous capacitance/return; the overall response reflects all three contributions."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"9790c5616c9d3749e8d9b61458e28bdceb92935664a4f554c74486d8a1830722"},"q-625403300fc4":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Increase peripheral arterial resistance","explanation":"Beta-2 stimulation relaxes vascular smooth muscle, generally reducing rather than increasing peripheral arteriolar resistance; beta-1 stimulation increases cardiac activity.","optionReasons":{"B":"Beta-2 stimulation relaxes vascular smooth muscle, generally reducing rather than increasing peripheral arteriolar resistance; beta-1 stimulation increases cardiac activity."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"74b1f95071e69485339658a4340b6c210dc908b0e9bbccd937e687ee4095d0f4"},"q-3d86c6e59ae4":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Αlfa agonists cause miosis","explanation":"Alpha-1 stimulation contracts the iris radial dilator muscle, causing mydriasis rather than miosis; beta blockade decreases aqueous humor production.","optionReasons":{"A":"Alpha-1 stimulation contracts the iris radial dilator muscle, causing mydriasis rather than miosis; beta blockade decreases aqueous humor production."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"e798f8870d75188a59bbd68287ea478791ae94b35dcbbe2ede5db91037d587eb"},"q-f951a6f332ed":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Methoxamine","explanation":"Methoxamine is an alpha-1-adrenergic agonist, not a beta-receptor agonist; epinephrine, isoproterenol and dobutamine have beta activity.","optionReasons":{"C":"Methoxamine is an alpha-1-adrenergic agonist, not a beta-receptor agonist; epinephrine, isoproterenol and dobutamine have beta activity."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"27669af7ac66735b43ae5938989cee586bcd0550af45cfbef8991d74a72afe57"},"q-537774185bd5":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Terbutaline","explanation":"Terbutaline preferentially stimulates beta-2 receptors to relax bronchial smooth muscle, producing less beta-1 cardiac stimulation than isoproterenol at usual doses.","optionReasons":{"B":"Terbutaline preferentially stimulates beta-2 receptors to relax bronchial smooth muscle, producing less beta-1 cardiac stimulation than isoproterenol at usual doses."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"4612821e960547986f7e27483de05b60422390467f5d231445275996d0800a27"},"q-05ed63564c88":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Stimulation of insulin secretion","explanation":"Alpha-2 receptor activation inhibits rather than stimulates insulin secretion from pancreatic beta cells; the other responses are recognized alpha-adrenoceptor effects.","optionReasons":{"C":"Alpha-2 receptor activation inhibits rather than stimulates insulin secretion from pancreatic beta cells; the other responses are recognized alpha-adrenoceptor effects."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"f2ad2d18b0ddcce52ac5a577d38923b76585e48d77ca04f13bff42df97228c5b"},"q-9643d43e2875":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Stimulation of renin secretion","explanation":"Renin release is chiefly stimulated by beta-1 receptors on renal juxtaglomerular cells, not beta-2 receptors. Beta-2 activation can shift potassium intracellularly and relax the uterus.","optionReasons":{"A":"Renin release is chiefly stimulated by beta-1 receptors on renal juxtaglomerular cells, not beta-2 receptors. Beta-2 activation can shift potassium intracellularly and relax the uterus."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"45ceeac5b55fc75cc03a65f797e1a4245c557e9283f1b529f1aa9e0e2fad67c7"},"q-f55277e1a556":{"correct":"D","answerText":"All of the above","explanation":"Epinephrine can raise glucose through beta-mediated glycogenolysis and gluconeogenesis and alpha-2-mediated inhibition of pancreatic insulin release.","optionReasons":{"D":"Epinephrine can raise glucose through beta-mediated glycogenolysis and gluconeogenesis and alpha-2-mediated inhibition of pancreatic insulin release."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"5e8d0f1b6ae609dd7762accf3f6b5e68c0b0fdab0e3e030a1281893ef15a7ba6"},"q-194dcfc29581":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Lipolysis","explanation":"Beta-3 receptor activation is associated especially with adipocyte lipolysis and bladder-detrusor relaxation rather than beta-2 bronchodilation or beta-1 cardiac acceleration.","optionReasons":{"A":"Beta-3 receptor activation is associated especially with adipocyte lipolysis and bladder-detrusor relaxation rather than beta-2 bronchodilation or beta-1 cardiac acceleration."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"f42796b07870d77ca78d8abb7d0fb933faf1fe0fa615279ba77877e8173705c3"},"q-0691cbda2dcc":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Norepinephrine has a predominantly beta action","explanation":"Norepinephrine mainly stimulates alpha-1, alpha-2 and beta-1 receptors, with relatively weak beta-2 effects; describing its action as predominantly beta is incorrect.","optionReasons":{"B":"Norepinephrine mainly stimulates alpha-1, alpha-2 and beta-1 receptors, with relatively weak beta-2 effects; describing its action as predominantly beta is incorrect."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"6487d4ec0f4d2ce4ff5a28f0bec2e4891110fd49725e8ab2bcb1aaeb2ee232d7"},"q-1f6e76bc706c":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Norepinephrine","explanation":"Norepinephrine directly activates both alpha and beta-1 receptors. Methoxamine acts mainly at alpha-1 receptors and isoproterenol acts at beta receptors, while ephedrine has mixed mechanisms.","optionReasons":{"A":"Norepinephrine directly activates both alpha and beta-1 receptors. Methoxamine acts mainly at alpha-1 receptors and isoproterenol acts at beta receptors, while ephedrine has mixed mechanisms."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"99d849484fa7e56cdde3b24aba6ea7bb7ebcfb37aa87c4d2648ca684444eaeb1"},"q-ef9c01a144f2":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Epinephrine","explanation":"Epinephrine stimulates alpha-1, alpha-2, beta-1 and beta-2 receptors. Selective beta-2 drugs and norepinephrine lack this same balanced four-receptor pattern.","optionReasons":{"C":"Epinephrine stimulates alpha-1, alpha-2, beta-1 and beta-2 receptors. Selective beta-2 drugs and norepinephrine lack this same balanced four-receptor pattern."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"5a6d124ca876fbbcb3e53d61510e6611d2befe692c117499450943cdad181112"},"q-c8f27b8c9bd3":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Norepinephrine","explanation":"Norepinephrine is a direct agonist at alpha-1, alpha-2 and beta-1 adrenergic receptors and has little beta-2 activity.","optionReasons":{"D":"Norepinephrine is a direct agonist at alpha-1, alpha-2 and beta-1 adrenergic receptors and has little beta-2 activity."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"cc1c56f542fd2e1792a33296c44c6198fe33943ca0ea2b4dea36cfa5741b15c6"},"q-d2fd16c1c302":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Xylometazoline","explanation":"Xylometazoline is an imidazoline-derived topical nasal decongestant with alpha-adrenoceptor agonist activity including alpha-2; the other drugs have different primary selectivities.","optionReasons":{"A":"Xylometazoline is an imidazoline-derived topical nasal decongestant with alpha-adrenoceptor agonist activity including alpha-2; the other drugs have different primary selectivities."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"84d1fe65b3c86fb8835a334c1721bb5c4434e9805469f5df640156d3424cdeb7"},"q-1f067358fc83":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Isoproterenol","explanation":"Isoproterenol activates both beta-1 and beta-2 adrenoceptors and is the classic nonselective beta agonist.","optionReasons":{"C":"Isoproterenol activates both beta-1 and beta-2 adrenoceptors and is the classic nonselective beta agonist."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"f3461a88297871f326ad182443210c7ec7535d3439b148b2ad5cd82489200fc2"},"q-56236c5e3318":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Dobutamine","explanation":"Dobutamine is predominantly a beta-1 cardiac agonist, improving myocardial inotropy; isoproterenol and epinephrine activate several adrenergic subtypes.","optionReasons":{"B":"Dobutamine is predominantly a beta-1 cardiac agonist, improving myocardial inotropy; isoproterenol and epinephrine activate several adrenergic subtypes."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"d96ef51d52a07c3a715854a378c41229c289b30d69efc1f712e3c3c2619d64c3"},"q-36153513eef8":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Terbutaline","explanation":"Terbutaline is a selective beta-2 bronchodilator, while isoproterenol is nonselective and dobutamine primarily stimulates beta-1 cardiac receptors.","optionReasons":{"A":"Terbutaline is a selective beta-2 bronchodilator, while isoproterenol is nonselective and dobutamine primarily stimulates beta-1 cardiac receptors."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"a0567a7a4434f163e8581f6836d0226a376a6e091c8e51a0ba2e8a6ec61bbfdd"},"q-0b68cbf8f646":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Ephedrine","explanation":"Ephedrine increases sympathetic neurotransmitter action largely through release of stored norepinephrine, in addition to its direct agonist effects, unlike the purely direct agents listed.","optionReasons":{"C":"Ephedrine increases sympathetic neurotransmitter action largely through release of stored norepinephrine, in addition to its direct agonist effects, unlike the purely direct agents listed."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"c8fb190b12f54aa7085fa41fdf75d6092b6960cac8ddb14bf30b2472c569fc94"},"q-5adb6676870a":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Predominance of alfa effects at low concentration","explanation":"Low epinephrine concentrations can favor beta-2 vasodilation; alpha-1 vasoconstriction dominates at higher doses, so the statement reversing that dose relationship is wrong.","optionReasons":{"C":"Low epinephrine concentrations can favor beta-2 vasodilation; alpha-1 vasoconstriction dominates at higher doses, so the statement reversing that dose relationship is wrong."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"6384d4db8cd03599b2759c49a261b76ed09208fedf4577a40f5c5b8e8445da10"},"q-31797035774f":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Decrease in oxygen consumption","explanation":"Epinephrine generally increases metabolic activity and oxygen consumption through adrenergic stimulation rather than decreasing them; bronchodilation and hyperglycemia are recognized effects.","optionReasons":{"A":"Epinephrine generally increases metabolic activity and oxygen consumption through adrenergic stimulation rather than decreasing them; bronchodilation and hyperglycemia are recognized effects."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"f2ea5c547c7d5c0f5f2099025bcd6bda4853e2b826a2104f6f616202f79c5c74"},"q-8e2f58103f8f":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Decrease the mean pressure below normal before returning to the control value","explanation":"Norepinephrine is a potent alpha-mediated vasoconstrictor that raises both systolic and diastolic blood pressure; a fall below baseline mean pressure is not its characteristic response.","optionReasons":{"B":"Norepinephrine is a potent alpha-mediated vasoconstrictor that raises both systolic and diastolic blood pressure; a fall below baseline mean pressure is not its characteristic response."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"9b4fefb9fe090e76796af284d4eff6a1ecfde082d981656e17c9711e646591a2"},"q-1ebc1c68db87":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Vasoconstriction","explanation":"Norepinephrine stimulates vascular alpha-1 receptors and causes vasoconstriction; it is relatively weak at beta-2 receptors responsible for bronchodilation.","optionReasons":{"A":"Norepinephrine stimulates vascular alpha-1 receptors and causes vasoconstriction; it is relatively weak at beta-2 receptors responsible for bronchodilation."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"7cf7619f911136979aea255499485e51831ae467cbe5e42e334d207fa2071b53"},"q-f444b6b49ff0":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Phenylephrine","explanation":"Phenylephrine is a comparatively selective alpha-1 agonist useful for mydriasis without cycloplegia, decongestion and vasopressor effects.","optionReasons":{"C":"Phenylephrine is a comparatively selective alpha-1 agonist useful for mydriasis without cycloplegia, decongestion and vasopressor effects."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"d43f7e3b7ea49bda42a3e404a43834059e70cb4584797daa836afd46b4677901"},"q-e59477a7c836":{"correct":"B","answerText":"It increases heart rate, contractility and cardiac output","explanation":"Methoxamine primarily increases vascular resistance via alpha-1 activation, usually triggering reflex bradycardia rather than directly increasing cardiac rate and contractility.","optionReasons":{"B":"Methoxamine primarily increases vascular resistance via alpha-1 activation, usually triggering reflex bradycardia rather than directly increasing cardiac rate and contractility."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"afa53307af028d77a3f0804749089e9c7edefba3dcea862e691287c17f0e3908"},"q-3f0a8555c768":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Xylometazoline","explanation":"Xylometazoline produces nasal mucosal vasoconstriction through topical alpha-adrenergic stimulation, including alpha-2 receptor activity.","optionReasons":{"A":"Xylometazoline produces nasal mucosal vasoconstriction through topical alpha-adrenergic stimulation, including alpha-2 receptor activity."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"4a1c1b0b1dbf29949a03fed6ef6b5f4d7cb3c38186b43731925e5fcc4e6481da"},"q-682bd34f57dd":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Nonselective beta receptor agonist","explanation":"Isoproterenol is a nonselective beta-1/beta-2 agonist with negligible alpha activity, producing cardiac stimulation and vascular/bronchial smooth-muscle relaxation.","optionReasons":{"D":"Isoproterenol is a nonselective beta-1/beta-2 agonist with negligible alpha activity, producing cardiac stimulation and vascular/bronchial smooth-muscle relaxation."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"929dd929dd92281d65e53fc89f61d4698a5a00c15babba43c0a278c217b9ac34"},"q-114e2c10dac5":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Bronchoconstriction","explanation":"Isoproterenol relaxes rather than constricts bronchial smooth muscle through beta-2 receptors, while its beta-1 effects increase heart rate and contractility.","optionReasons":{"C":"Isoproterenol relaxes rather than constricts bronchial smooth muscle through beta-2 receptors, while its beta-1 effects increase heart rate and contractility."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"f02271b9a8fd0ce297aa152fb25543a67435c5517367d80b62a43ea818cfcf54"},"q-228eb80c4440":{"correct":"B","answerText":"It is used to treat bronchospasm","explanation":"Dobutamine is used for short-term cardiac inotropic support rather than routine relief of bronchospasm; selective beta-2 agonists are used for bronchial relaxation.","optionReasons":{"B":"Dobutamine is used for short-term cardiac inotropic support rather than routine relief of bronchospasm; selective beta-2 agonists are used for bronchial relaxation."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"54468f0a0da8c48b6aa5532d211462c527df6ec02f0c9dd098a796d7a875d241"},"q-f069800d32b6":{"correct":"D","answerText":"It decreases arterial pressure","explanation":"Ephedrine usually raises blood pressure by adrenergic stimulation; it does not characteristically lower arterial pressure.","optionReasons":{"D":"Ephedrine usually raises blood pressure by adrenergic stimulation; it does not characteristically lower arterial pressure."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"45a5167da7703caf215d23cdcd9e1fa0841423849a4e8339f058587cde848cfc"},"q-9a2dab783ec1":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Bronchodilation","explanation":"Ephedrine has mixed sympathomimetic actions and can cause bronchodilation, cardiac stimulation and increased blood pressure rather than hypotension or bradycardia.","optionReasons":{"B":"Ephedrine has mixed sympathomimetic actions and can cause bronchodilation, cardiac stimulation and increased blood pressure rather than hypotension or bradycardia."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"69751dcb5802bcff8756e40e613c7f617075d4b829e43453975512486f0afcfd"},"q-dad1cead0ef5":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Ephedrine","explanation":"Ephedrine has historically been used as an orally active vasopressor for orthostatic hypotension. This is a pharmacology-identification question, not a recommendation for current first-line treatment.","optionReasons":{"C":"Ephedrine has historically been used as an orally active vasopressor for orthostatic hypotension. This is a pharmacology-identification question, not a recommendation for current first-line treatment."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"c3311ed0992b0caeb2f82d3b15c169b649170efce0746ecb0b68e8570be8495a"},"q-7b9678e675b4":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Phenylephrine","explanation":"Phenylephrine is a directly acting alpha-1 vasoconstrictor used to raise vascular tone and blood pressure in selected acute settings.","optionReasons":{"D":"Phenylephrine is a directly acting alpha-1 vasoconstrictor used to raise vascular tone and blood pressure in selected acute settings."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"bcc90036655aa51ae0f54e12132a0e3c115df023ad39a41cd55df68bf021c392"},"q-888d7e16fda7":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Phenylephrine","explanation":"Phenylephrine is a short-acting topical alpha-adrenergic nasal decongestant, in contrast to longer-acting agents such as xylometazoline.","optionReasons":{"C":"Phenylephrine is a short-acting topical alpha-adrenergic nasal decongestant, in contrast to longer-acting agents such as xylometazoline."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"c6873ea2dc1b620cd419ade0ad271680a7a4a67619660e9547ea2d525cb155d6"},"q-315f70a27afd":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Xylometazoline","explanation":"Xylometazoline is a longer-acting topical nasal decongestant with vasoconstrictor effects lasting longer than phenylephrine.","optionReasons":{"D":"Xylometazoline is a longer-acting topical nasal decongestant with vasoconstrictor effects lasting longer than phenylephrine."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"06eb02c8ab208ff2f7109d6f26c72159893792e3f17d2091ab3a75a4f0e87028"},"q-5fc58db93eae":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Xylometazoline","explanation":"Xylometazoline is a nasal alpha-adrenergic agonist used for topical decongestion; the other options are not alpha-2-selective topical nasal agents.","optionReasons":{"B":"Xylometazoline is a nasal alpha-adrenergic agonist used for topical decongestion; the other options are not alpha-2-selective topical nasal agents."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"50c10c77e44abb5cb63850db93ac29d93e2d5f3207f624cf72e7ef7980057862"},"q-8bab1939f920":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Phenylephrine","explanation":"Phenylephrine contracts the iris radial dilator muscle through alpha-1 receptors, producing mydriasis without significant cycloplegia.","optionReasons":{"B":"Phenylephrine contracts the iris radial dilator muscle through alpha-1 receptors, producing mydriasis without significant cycloplegia."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"fbd88772ecb50a3f127c317230b2da2573ea2883b0e3a7961f2c3e14f41ab433"},"q-30e40f541275":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Drug-induced parkinsonism","explanation":"Serious sympathomimetic toxicities include myocardial ischemia, arrhythmias and severe hypertension; drug-induced parkinsonism is characteristic of dopamine blockade, not adrenergic stimulation.","optionReasons":{"A":"Serious sympathomimetic toxicities include myocardial ischemia, arrhythmias and severe hypertension; drug-induced parkinsonism is characteristic of dopamine blockade, not adrenergic stimulation."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"f3924a1d3088fe750f2c2cf94ab8c29902cafee160a3aceba4093b860f07759a"},"q-e64983d9b86e":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Phentolamine","explanation":"Phentolamine competitively blocks both alpha-1 and alpha-2 adrenoceptors; prazosin is alpha-1-selective and metoprolol is beta-1-selective.","optionReasons":{"B":"Phentolamine competitively blocks both alpha-1 and alpha-2 adrenoceptors; prazosin is alpha-1-selective and metoprolol is beta-1-selective."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"a88af929e613ff1486d79cdc8bb30ec0b104a3fd5cd87762e0fe95a6be25a2c6"},"q-ff90f95f9542":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Prazosin","explanation":"Prazosin selectively antagonizes alpha-1 receptors, causing vascular smooth-muscle relaxation and reduced peripheral resistance.","optionReasons":{"C":"Prazosin selectively antagonizes alpha-1 receptors, causing vascular smooth-muscle relaxation and reduced peripheral resistance."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"2ddc7242b40b04aa8208caa9cc19d999bbd7a8bfc47c186508789d15381fce23"},"q-a63dc7ad5906":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Phenoxybenzamine","explanation":"Phenoxybenzamine alkylates alpha receptors, causing long-lasting irreversible nonselective alpha blockade.","optionReasons":{"D":"Phenoxybenzamine alkylates alpha receptors, causing long-lasting irreversible nonselective alpha blockade."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"009932ed6889f95184252e72505a71be92c842666117e69c1fa1c716f0d947ef"},"q-075eded1ec1f":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Propranolol","explanation":"Propranolol blocks both beta-1 and beta-2 adrenoceptors; atenolol and metoprolol are relatively beta-1 selective.","optionReasons":{"C":"Propranolol blocks both beta-1 and beta-2 adrenoceptors; atenolol and metoprolol are relatively beta-1 selective."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"b011a875b58b2b2c25eb3adf3785818e4f3c622e056781a15d49e81236cc1545"},"q-8c313cba7b3d":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Metoprolol","explanation":"Metoprolol is a relatively selective beta-1 receptor antagonist at usual doses, unlike the nonselective propranolol or sotalol.","optionReasons":{"B":"Metoprolol is a relatively selective beta-1 receptor antagonist at usual doses, unlike the nonselective propranolol or sotalol."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"1def9517880fae2ea6cc2c2bcc9911ffefd06b5d6d065b201b9d0743c7139573"},"q-eb303f187463":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Butoxamine","explanation":"Butoxamine is a pharmacological beta-2-selective receptor antagonist used mainly as an experimental agent rather than a standard treatment drug.","optionReasons":{"D":"Butoxamine is a pharmacological beta-2-selective receptor antagonist used mainly as an experimental agent rather than a standard treatment drug."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"d401118dbda1f21b70091cb27ab87350a2651f47130557227bd98c2ffa7ef5db"},"q-2c8e74f30202":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Pindolol","explanation":"Pindolol is a beta blocker with intrinsic sympathomimetic activity, meaning partial agonism at beta receptors while blocking stronger catecholamine stimulation.","optionReasons":{"C":"Pindolol is a beta blocker with intrinsic sympathomimetic activity, meaning partial agonism at beta receptors while blocking stronger catecholamine stimulation."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"3642b7a19d0980f1a59643927185cd0e697bd8521af9baeec163805419d137b1"},"q-1476d3b3f7ca":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Labetalol","explanation":"Labetalol blocks beta receptors and alpha-1 receptors reversibly, thereby combining reduced cardiac adrenergic activity with vasodilation.","optionReasons":{"A":"Labetalol blocks beta receptors and alpha-1 receptors reversibly, thereby combining reduced cardiac adrenergic activity with vasodilation."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"aadf84eda5d0fc6fa2dcccdb680e3a3fcb38c692cf09d88fa0b7c17ab426dbd4"},"q-328f0c70f1dc":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Reserpine","explanation":"Reserpine impairs monoamine storage in vesicles and indirectly reduces adrenergic neurotransmission rather than competitively blocking adrenoceptors.","optionReasons":{"B":"Reserpine impairs monoamine storage in vesicles and indirectly reduces adrenergic neurotransmission rather than competitively blocking adrenoceptors."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"4d4310fc825a76fdfb34423b9138d8af702a3e96136b3df7a39718654b94d165"},"q-ec08643ae18e":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Reversible or irreversible interaction with adrenoreceptors","explanation":"Alpha and beta antagonists primarily inhibit catecholamine binding and signaling at adrenoceptors through reversible or irreversible receptor blockade.","optionReasons":{"A":"Alpha and beta antagonists primarily inhibit catecholamine binding and signaling at adrenoceptors through reversible or irreversible receptor blockade."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"64bec2b235a2bb2c4d14ef021d23350073b68a432a5f737eb51a166e6cc81bfc"},"q-b3117b93bb65":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Bronchospasm","explanation":"Bronchospasm results from beta-2 antagonism, not alpha blockade; alpha antagonists instead reduce vasoconstrictor tone and may cause orthostatic hypotension.","optionReasons":{"C":"Bronchospasm results from beta-2 antagonism, not alpha blockade; alpha antagonists instead reduce vasoconstrictor tone and may cause orthostatic hypotension."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"961750bcff69c4854bd1bc6e07b330e49b46f15ccb33317aedfdce4c51a6b822"},"q-bdb5809b2945":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Phentolamine","explanation":"Phentolamine is an imidazoline-derived competitive antagonist of alpha-1 and alpha-2 receptors.","optionReasons":{"D":"Phentolamine is an imidazoline-derived competitive antagonist of alpha-1 and alpha-2 receptors."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"3aeb4a7b6760217b0b7e0f8b6cadbf98d5976a59c7bc48f0efdcf9750401f090"},"q-b1ee14797222":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Antagonism of presynaptic alfa2 receptors enhances norepinephrine release, which causes cardiac stimulation via unblocked beta receptors 31","explanation":"Blocking presynaptic alpha-2 autoreceptors increases norepinephrine release, which can stimulate unblocked cardiac beta-1 receptors and provoke tachycardia.","optionReasons":{"A":"Blocking presynaptic alpha-2 autoreceptors increases norepinephrine release, which can stimulate unblocked cardiac beta-1 receptors and provoke tachycardia."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"3b1842a193c9c7ee13bb46df15a2f4ed84521ad86a1eff61288c04ecdeb668aa"},"q-37577725b5d3":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Pheochromocytoma","explanation":"Nonselective alpha blockade counteracts catecholamine-mediated vasoconstriction in pheochromocytoma; these agents are not therapies for asthma or arrhythmias.","optionReasons":{"C":"Nonselective alpha blockade counteracts catecholamine-mediated vasoconstriction in pheochromocytoma; these agents are not therapies for asthma or arrhythmias."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"c81e668349d5a01bfaf281c782aa4b3c71fd9ac7478607b8bfe135e1330dd629"},"q-074631eb844e":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Phentolamine","explanation":"Phentolamine is a competitive alpha antagonist that can reverse catecholamine-related vasoconstriction in pheochromocytoma, particularly acute hypertensive episodes.","optionReasons":{"C":"Phentolamine is a competitive alpha antagonist that can reverse catecholamine-related vasoconstriction in pheochromocytoma, particularly acute hypertensive episodes."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"dea3d7a0ba3115eb3a37699003b2c165d782d2be3628ac09f60717ca33a44962"},"q-0726be31a4cd":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Bradycardia","explanation":"Phentolamine can cause tachycardia and occasionally arrhythmias or ischemia; bradycardia is not a typical principal adverse reaction.","optionReasons":{"B":"Phentolamine can cause tachycardia and occasionally arrhythmias or ischemia; bradycardia is not a typical principal adverse reaction."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"26fdc0a7733c17057dc5fbff9af55e87f76cafdcfda26f9c052a11229876045d"},"q-1304ca4b5d8b":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Phenoxybenzamine","explanation":"Phenoxybenzamine forms covalent bonds with alpha-adrenoceptors, yielding irreversible prolonged blockade until new receptors are synthesized.","optionReasons":{"B":"Phenoxybenzamine forms covalent bonds with alpha-adrenoceptors, yielding irreversible prolonged blockade until new receptors are synthesized."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"eeee31c83e1f4d6dfc5934b821a5d4c98081727ea58b075791bf721d58d6d559"},"q-cc77cf89d27b":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Irreversible blockade of alfa receptors","explanation":"Prazosin is a competitive reversible alpha-1 blocker, so irreversible receptor blockade is not a property distinguishing it from phentolamine.","optionReasons":{"A":"Prazosin is a competitive reversible alpha-1 blocker, so irreversible receptor blockade is not a property distinguishing it from phentolamine."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"be129392aca1dc09a808565f7b28849f6ad9ce6e8df03378d87e10a06c0f37fc"},"q-90c119601347":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Tamsulosin","explanation":"Tamsulosin preferentially blocks alpha-1A receptors in the prostate and bladder neck, helping relieve lower-urinary-tract symptoms of BPH.","optionReasons":{"B":"Tamsulosin preferentially blocks alpha-1A receptors in the prostate and bladder neck, helping relieve lower-urinary-tract symptoms of BPH."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"ab45b32a1436d27b2b90f3d316bb9825b1e7c71e379d981eeaecad574b2e34e4"},"q-e43cd777e525":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Benign prostatic hyperplasia (BPH)","explanation":"Alpha-1 blockers such as tamsulosin and alfuzosin relax prostatic and bladder-neck smooth muscle to improve urinary outflow in benign prostatic hyperplasia.","optionReasons":{"C":"Alpha-1 blockers such as tamsulosin and alfuzosin relax prostatic and bladder-neck smooth muscle to improve urinary outflow in benign prostatic hyperplasia."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"3f62c1f715a33f2e4cabd6058ff8a5e1598025a7751f0d7c1b3e0a8a909c32aa"},"q-4ef8cd2483c3":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Prazosin","explanation":"Prazosin is a selective alpha-1 antagonist that lowers systemic vascular resistance and can lower blood pressure in hypertension; nonselective alpha blockers are generally not routine antihypertensive agents.","optionReasons":{"D":"Prazosin is a selective alpha-1 antagonist that lowers systemic vascular resistance and can lower blood pressure in hypertension; nonselective alpha blockers are generally not routine antihypertensive agents."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"ec377d47b3585cd054a5ecb025e3e1649ffa88be1ab919797dfa756927649f77"},"q-2d97167ae2db":{"correct":"D","answerText":"All of the above","explanation":"Beta blockade can lower blood pressure through reduced cardiac output, suppression of renal renin release and changes in vascular hemodynamics over time.","optionReasons":{"D":"Beta blockade can lower blood pressure through reduced cardiac output, suppression of renal renin release and changes in vascular hemodynamics over time."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"9453315eaad02e65d3c40e20cd4ac360b7923f9d60d1d4d88db2be62273b441d"},"q-d074ea737626":{"correct":"C","answerText":"They induce depression and depleted stores of catecholamines","explanation":"Beta antagonists block catecholamine signaling at beta receptors; they do not ordinarily lower blood pressure by depleting stored catecholamines, which is a different mechanism exemplified by reserpine.","optionReasons":{"C":"Beta antagonists block catecholamine signaling at beta receptors; they do not ordinarily lower blood pressure by depleting stored catecholamines, which is a different mechanism exemplified by reserpine."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"400c53637794d69da64fc8d4ebf77ade1f8949c2c128971071ec9b46ee4b750d"},"q-7fa99db7c5bc":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Acute effects of these drugs include a fall in peripheral resistance","explanation":"Acute beta-2 blockade can increase rather than decrease peripheral vascular resistance, even while beta-1 blockade reduces cardiac activity and renin release.","optionReasons":{"B":"Acute beta-2 blockade can increase rather than decrease peripheral vascular resistance, even while beta-1 blockade reduces cardiac activity and renin release."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"3e7ede0f057ac64134674e5eb72d44e980cfd0f64ddc856fdee964699ca0ac6c"},"q-6d2df3a637d2":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Increase plasma concentrations of HDL and decrease of VLDL","explanation":"Older nonselective beta blockers can raise triglycerides and lower HDL cholesterol; increasing HDL while decreasing VLDL is not their typical lipid effect.","optionReasons":{"A":"Older nonselective beta blockers can raise triglycerides and lower HDL cholesterol; increasing HDL while decreasing VLDL is not their typical lipid effect."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"924b59f6d953bf128a28492610a78fcf588df783206520420fdaa075e59a5afc"},"q-019019e18c84":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Inhibition of glycogenolysis","explanation":"Beta blockade can suppress beta-mediated hepatic glycogenolysis, which is particularly relevant to recognition and recovery from hypoglycemia in insulin-treated patients.","optionReasons":{"C":"Beta blockade can suppress beta-mediated hepatic glycogenolysis, which is particularly relevant to recognition and recovery from hypoglycemia in insulin-treated patients."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"e89b940e3c1c3b7209b630c7951790824a6ad2e1d99cc31adee95f363ff0c003"},"q-7da39d727066":{"correct":"B","answerText":"It reduces blood flow to the brain","explanation":"Propranolol reduces myocardial oxygen demand, renin release and AV nodal conduction; reducing brain blood flow is not one of its established therapeutic cardiac actions.","optionReasons":{"B":"Propranolol reduces myocardial oxygen demand, renin release and AV nodal conduction; reducing brain blood flow is not one of its established therapeutic cardiac actions."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"080f31647c86ffdf10c637b543fe60d7c971834971562128bb708bb009f242c0"},"q-9d342e984efb":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Hyperglycemia","explanation":"Propranolol can impair glycogenolytic recovery from hypoglycemia and mask adrenergic warning signs, so hyperglycemia is not the characteristic adverse effect being sought.","optionReasons":{"C":"Propranolol can impair glycogenolytic recovery from hypoglycemia and mask adrenergic warning signs, so hyperglycemia is not the characteristic adverse effect being sought."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"205f3187386dc317ed7283a1c32c99de2385fa6dc1dcbf5c8e873e63f612378b"},"q-b75d703fe230":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Bronchial asthma","explanation":"Nonselective beta antagonism can provoke bronchospasm, making propranolol inappropriate for treating bronchial asthma despite its uses for cardiovascular conditions, thyroid symptoms and migraine prevention.","optionReasons":{"D":"Nonselective beta antagonism can provoke bronchospasm, making propranolol inappropriate for treating bronchial asthma despite its uses for cardiovascular conditions, thyroid symptoms and migraine prevention."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"b2f13a21285099036c882306ba6a3abde04d441687a9a6be75866fd9948f9a17"},"q-0b47d2bd8c00":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Are members of the beta1-selective group","explanation":"Metoprolol and atenolol are relatively beta-1-selective antagonists. Their selectivity is dose dependent and does not imply complete absence of bronchial beta-2 blockade.","optionReasons":{"A":"Metoprolol and atenolol are relatively beta-1-selective antagonists. Their selectivity is dose dependent and does not imply complete absence of bronchial beta-2 blockade."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"40f7198588842ddd6cdc3f8adddb8ad0f270e3d294be6cbaba6876a77dee3d83"},"q-628989d855f1":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Metoprolol 33","explanation":"Metoprolol is relatively beta-1 selective and therefore has less bronchial beta-2 blockade than nonselective propranolol, nadolol or timolol, although caution is still required in asthma.","optionReasons":{"B":"Metoprolol is relatively beta-1 selective and therefore has less bronchial beta-2 blockade than nonselective propranolol, nadolol or timolol, although caution is still required in asthma."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"8be47c4a2fa0bf2ac889f947f656fa4c8b667082989d3179382110ce62cf1bea"},"q-16d01e54a3c9":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Nadolol","explanation":"Nadolol has a relatively long elimination half-life and often permits once-daily dosing, unlike the shorter acting propranolol and metoprolol preparations.","optionReasons":{"C":"Nadolol has a relatively long elimination half-life and often permits once-daily dosing, unlike the shorter acting propranolol and metoprolol preparations."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"daf24db183edc452d2d44d1c06a9b497bdcec705de4bf2d0bc74e03a52895b77"},"q-b8f54d42893e":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Betaxolol","explanation":"Betaxolol is a comparatively long-acting beta-1-selective antagonist; nadolol is long acting but is not beta-1 selective.","optionReasons":{"A":"Betaxolol is a comparatively long-acting beta-1-selective antagonist; nadolol is long acting but is not beta-1 selective."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"543d2aa19d79aeee8c393510aaab220fd7f8c8a202b704d2d09d2e6b7bfa8598"},"q-8f10e29ebb38":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Oxprenolol","explanation":"Oxprenolol exhibits intrinsic sympathomimetic activity, meaning partial beta agonism despite its clinically predominant antagonism.","optionReasons":{"B":"Oxprenolol exhibits intrinsic sympathomimetic activity, meaning partial beta agonism despite its clinically predominant antagonism."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"2b78c321ef1e592dd79fdd3a0ebdf42e3edd8db2945acf13e34ec8f335dc077f"},"q-ac223d8e51cd":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Labetalol","explanation":"Labetalol blocks beta-1, beta-2 and alpha-1 receptors, reducing cardiac adrenergic effects while also producing alpha-1-mediated vasodilation.","optionReasons":{"A":"Labetalol blocks beta-1, beta-2 and alpha-1 receptors, reducing cardiac adrenergic effects while also producing alpha-1-mediated vasodilation."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"b24e335f17eb6dd7188e80ccbc11393c3c578c9c77dc1fd0b38cfb95806d9b11"},"q-7da9aa292e59":{"correct":"A","answerText":"It is a beta1-selective antagonist","explanation":"Carvedilol is a nonselective beta antagonist with alpha-1-blocking activity, not a beta-1-selective blocker; antioxidant effects have also been described.","optionReasons":{"A":"Carvedilol is a nonselective beta antagonist with alpha-1-blocking activity, not a beta-1-selective blocker; antioxidant effects have also been described."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"ca5e9e018b2eff0f6aa28d990a8eedf1b9aa4d5712beaef8c1bf638b00760f7f"},"q-a98c204685fc":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Reserpine","explanation":"Reserpine is an alkaloid obtained from Rauwolfia that inhibits vesicular monoamine transporter activity, depleting catecholamine and serotonin stores.","optionReasons":{"C":"Reserpine is an alkaloid obtained from Rauwolfia that inhibits vesicular monoamine transporter activity, depleting catecholamine and serotonin stores."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"e371b2f91ffdd47f5d6a7707530ffba9c7dc12a13e0c35f9ada476a06460b483"},"q-9b9e504134f4":{"correct":"A","answerText":"It inhibits the uptake of norepinephrine into vesicles and MAO","explanation":"Reserpine inhibits vesicular monoamine uptake but does not directly inhibit monoamine oxidase; transmitter remaining outside vesicles is then degraded by monoamine oxidase.","optionReasons":{"A":"Reserpine inhibits vesicular monoamine uptake but does not directly inhibit monoamine oxidase; transmitter remaining outside vesicles is then degraded by monoamine oxidase."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"261f20624863a95e9864434b78ad01f9078c4ff131a4e8a506f44198a9799ec6"},"q-db6c467b42e4":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Sleep disorders","explanation":"Hypnotics induce or maintain sleep and are used for selected sleep disturbances rather than for core treatment of psychotic or Parkinsonian syndromes.","optionReasons":{"B":"Hypnotics induce or maintain sleep and are used for selected sleep disturbances rather than for core treatment of psychotic or Parkinsonian syndromes."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"1ac35af55cca9fbc0fad065ad4d34ccf32691ba3663fe666ba5de182f4a998c0"},"q-e6426b2b3b05":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Produce drowsiness, encourage the onset and maintenance of sleep","explanation":"A hypnotic is intended to promote sleep onset and/or maintenance, whereas anesthesia, anxiolysis and mood stabilization are separate pharmacological endpoints.","optionReasons":{"C":"A hypnotic is intended to promote sleep onset and/or maintenance, whereas anesthesia, anxiolysis and mood stabilization are separate pharmacological endpoints."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"06537b2c208a0701251ebf19425968440bc2f1399f6c1c9efb1a104f3f22f25d"},"q-fa75ab27de34":{"correct":"D","answerText":"All of the above","explanation":"Benzodiazepines, nonbenzodiazepine Z-drugs and barbiturates have all been used as hypnotics historically, although safety profiles and current preferences differ markedly.","optionReasons":{"D":"Benzodiazepines, nonbenzodiazepine Z-drugs and barbiturates have all been used as hypnotics historically, although safety profiles and current preferences differ markedly."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"5c669fed775e8253ed0b7e449bdd333a4d7a305558ebd84da3029209706d0c5a"},"q-3c5bbec96740":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Thyopental","explanation":"Thiopental is a thiobarbiturate derivative used intravenously as an anesthetic; the other listed agents are not barbiturates.","optionReasons":{"C":"Thiopental is a thiobarbiturate derivative used intravenously as an anesthetic; the other listed agents are not barbiturates."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"3045fb649e0e5975a923b95cf290aa163e2b4e900c96ac8c9b28fc03df3e4272"},"q-3c78fdab51de":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Zolpidem","explanation":"Zolpidem is an imidazopyridine nonbenzodiazepine hypnotic that positively modulates GABA-A receptor signaling through benzodiazepine-related binding sites.","optionReasons":{"C":"Zolpidem is an imidazopyridine nonbenzodiazepine hypnotic that positively modulates GABA-A receptor signaling through benzodiazepine-related binding sites."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"173dcc3e52de50604a63dff7bb7ac1961ceb3f9d574ef12dd1ed39735841093d"},"q-c4159af2e36a":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Phenobarbital","explanation":"Phenobarbital has a slower onset and longer duration than short-acting agents such as triazolam; it is unsuitable for routine insomnia treatment.","optionReasons":{"A":"Phenobarbital has a slower onset and longer duration than short-acting agents such as triazolam; it is unsuitable for routine insomnia treatment."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"6064c25c675423a1df2745d663a15cdd56853f2730dbd7862d6eb687ef77f50c"},"q-3cc9ab6b4af7":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Thiopental","explanation":"Thiopental is an ultra-short-acting intravenous barbiturate whose brief initial effect is mainly due to redistribution from the brain into peripheral tissues.","optionReasons":{"C":"Thiopental is an ultra-short-acting intravenous barbiturate whose brief initial effect is mainly due to redistribution from the brain into peripheral tissues."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"305a51d8c6c972dd7f514ec14b5c9276ef38e225ffe27e2c364ea0f6335dabb0"},"q-e29784cbb40b":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Phenobarbital","explanation":"Phenobarbital is a long-acting barbiturate with an elimination half-life often extending over several days, unlike thiopental or secobarbital.","optionReasons":{"C":"Phenobarbital is a long-acting barbiturate with an elimination half-life often extending over several days, unlike thiopental or secobarbital."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"3aaba3b439dbfbf9ab2d994a16f80a06be40ed32313d3888e592bdd8c5db4079"},"q-adc4a9ba45e4":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Triazolam","explanation":"Triazolam is a relatively short-acting hypnotic benzodiazepine compared with temazepam, diazepam or flurazepam and its active metabolites.","optionReasons":{"B":"Triazolam is a relatively short-acting hypnotic benzodiazepine compared with temazepam, diazepam or flurazepam and its active metabolites."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"d5ad1235b0635b659a156ae05f37cf7cebc18d5289621823e2cb1458ce820313"},"q-bce1117b1961":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Phenobarbital","explanation":"Phenobarbital has a long elimination half-life and is more likely to accumulate and cause residual daytime sedation than short-acting hypnotics.","optionReasons":{"C":"Phenobarbital has a long elimination half-life and is more likely to accumulate and cause residual daytime sedation than short-acting hypnotics."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"e186504661ea98751ffbbeabfac46546b59ec7cbd04cb4e168616aabd7648bae"},"q-dd7571f7c1e9":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Phenobarbital","explanation":"Phenobarbital induces several hepatic drug-metabolizing enzymes, including CYP enzymes, and can alter clearance of coadministered medicines.","optionReasons":{"A":"Phenobarbital induces several hepatic drug-metabolizing enzymes, including CYP enzymes, and can alter clearance of coadministered medicines."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"dc4fcdbc08df1e7ca4392e7c9871cdee1e24f7497385151ac4c66dfb00a117c4"},"q-a3f25a5b2935":{"correct":"D","answerText":"All of the above","explanation":"Unlike enzyme-inducing barbiturates, flurazepam, triazolam and zaleplon do not characteristically induce hepatic microsomal enzymes in clinical use.","optionReasons":{"D":"Unlike enzyme-inducing barbiturates, flurazepam, triazolam and zaleplon do not characteristically induce hepatic microsomal enzymes in clinical use."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"a8fb12c01b34afcee940556ad69448840753386a839941ddab5e457c2db11e2e"},"q-2b4ff72aa440":{"correct":"D","answerText":"All of the above","explanation":"Hepatic dysfunction, advancing age and interacting enzyme-inducing or inhibiting drugs can all modify hypnotic drug exposure and accumulation.","optionReasons":{"D":"Hepatic dysfunction, advancing age and interacting enzyme-inducing or inhibiting drugs can all modify hypnotic drug exposure and accumulation."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"849e6c757853589e8b925e1a67dc79c5d186a081ab611e5991eed11b29a30439"},"q-1f0be7bbf212":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Temazepam","explanation":"Temazepam undergoes mainly glucuronide conjugation and lacks long-lived active metabolites, making it comparatively preferable to long-acting barbiturates or flurazepam when a hypnotic is required in older adults.","optionReasons":{"C":"Temazepam undergoes mainly glucuronide conjugation and lacks long-lived active metabolites, making it comparatively preferable to long-acting barbiturates or flurazepam when a hypnotic is required in older adults."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"815c3ee59bb43c3c141913de9e22c6ca7987f8a8ceb19beda9438bd33809e224"},"q-c3469706d1ac":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Increasing the duration of the GABA-gated Cl- channel openings","explanation":"At hypnotic doses, barbiturates potentiate GABA-A receptors mainly by prolonging chloride-channel opening duration; benzodiazepines instead generally increase opening frequency.","optionReasons":{"A":"At hypnotic doses, barbiturates potentiate GABA-A receptors mainly by prolonging chloride-channel opening duration; benzodiazepines instead generally increase opening frequency."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"d7fb45355c8a4c33a494d92f5bb27b524345bac00b36c619af0b822ee0396ac0"},"q-0619c5ac1a4a":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Selective agonists of the BZ1 (omega1) subtype of BZ receptors","explanation":"Imidazopyridine hypnotics such as zolpidem act preferentially at the alpha-1-associated benzodiazepine binding site, historically called the BZ1 or omega-1 subtype.","optionReasons":{"B":"Imidazopyridine hypnotics such as zolpidem act preferentially at the alpha-1-associated benzodiazepine binding site, historically called the BZ1 or omega-1 subtype."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"e404026624aeb613d0295ecda861d00ccfd922850a9d5db8d14c13c97d9506a2"},"q-833c42371875":{"correct":"D","answerText":"All of the above","explanation":"Zaleplon, flurazepam and zolpidem all enhance inhibitory GABA-A receptor function as positive allosteric modulators despite belonging to different chemical groups.","optionReasons":{"D":"Zaleplon, flurazepam and zolpidem all enhance inhibitory GABA-A receptor function as positive allosteric modulators despite belonging to different chemical groups."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"52a13195985a0e606b2d74bf6a7b3f7195124bf954ad8ebc70f50070d0337b65"},"q-bdfc48411f1d":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Zolpidem 36","explanation":"Zolpidem preferentially acts at the BZ1/omega-1 subtype of the GABA-A benzodiazepine receptor complex; flumazenil is an antagonist.","optionReasons":{"B":"Zolpidem preferentially acts at the BZ1/omega-1 subtype of the GABA-A benzodiazepine receptor complex; flumazenil is an antagonist."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"dade98608b80156e35aff3b37870684cd4ba0305be00c61ce339a06f2f65b458"},"q-611e08566009":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Flurazepam","explanation":"Flurazepam is a conventional benzodiazepine that interacts with multiple benzodiazepine-sensitive GABA-A receptor subtypes, unlike relatively alpha-1-preferring Z-drugs.","optionReasons":{"C":"Flurazepam is a conventional benzodiazepine that interacts with multiple benzodiazepine-sensitive GABA-A receptor subtypes, unlike relatively alpha-1-preferring Z-drugs."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"ad60ddcfb08e7e7834fbf58ffd9ad8b977f65c069c6aa6ee7cfe430460829e2b"},"q-0cd7edb93bc4":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Flumazenil","explanation":"Flumazenil competitively antagonizes the benzodiazepine binding site on GABA-A receptors and can reverse selected benzodiazepine effects under clinical monitoring.","optionReasons":{"A":"Flumazenil competitively antagonizes the benzodiazepine binding site on GABA-A receptors and can reverse selected benzodiazepine effects under clinical monitoring."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"5b9bd54ef15f067f326f3d4b7240864c4b28c2eedcbd985d26a6843ecf0b4f7f"},"q-e4a5de9ded02":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Zolpidem","explanation":"Flumazenil can antagonize zolpidem, which acts at the benzodiazepine-sensitive site of GABA-A receptors; it does not reverse opioid or ethanol intoxication.","optionReasons":{"C":"Flumazenil can antagonize zolpidem, which acts at the benzodiazepine-sensitive site of GABA-A receptors; it does not reverse opioid or ethanol intoxication."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"bd6ad923dbf36b5daacb2ea005da587512d2eb775735d27ee0c57181b69fbe86"},"q-19f1681cc998":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Bicuculline","explanation":"Bicuculline is a competitive antagonist at the GABA-A receptor GABA-binding site, unlike flurazepam and zolpidem, which facilitate GABA action.","optionReasons":{"B":"Bicuculline is a competitive antagonist at the GABA-A receptor GABA-binding site, unlike flurazepam and zolpidem, which facilitate GABA action."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"c0b05929f54e5c9bbae7522410b2e814861f25c5979c5ddc56c10ed9076bdc10"},"q-776c58f5d493":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Picrotoxin","explanation":"Picrotoxin blocks the GABA-A receptor chloride-channel pore rather than the benzodiazepine recognition site.","optionReasons":{"D":"Picrotoxin blocks the GABA-A receptor chloride-channel pore rather than the benzodiazepine recognition site."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"73deebdb067a8c99a3d9b1830a3f2bc6949cb194a78012a6bc829fbf2a0a841e"},"q-616e2b4e679f":{"correct":"D","answerText":"All of the above","explanation":"Barbiturates have a narrow therapeutic index, substantial overdose toxicity and dependence potential, and can strongly perturb normal sleep architecture; safer classes displaced them from routine insomnia therapy.","optionReasons":{"D":"Barbiturates have a narrow therapeutic index, substantial overdose toxicity and dependence potential, and can strongly perturb normal sleep architecture; safer classes displaced them from routine insomnia therapy."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"3dbbd6a4103ca6fe5bc7ae9e8d72df4a62acee56e036e69a601f32ad0312ce37"},"q-7b1bdea2ffd2":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Flurazepam","explanation":"Flurazepam was specifically developed and used as a hypnotic benzodiazepine; clonazepam is primarily an antiseizure agent and lorazepam has broader anxiolytic uses.","optionReasons":{"C":"Flurazepam was specifically developed and used as a hypnotic benzodiazepine; clonazepam is primarily an antiseizure agent and lorazepam has broader anxiolytic uses."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"a3863c0df9cbe10cca5edd63d8ae02ae2d68e701d3441be3e492a38e4d189546"},"q-df8ecd297959":{"correct":"D","answerText":"All of the above","explanation":"An ideal hypnotic acts quickly enough to facilitate sleep, lasts appropriately, preserves sleep architecture and causes minimal residual impairment the following day.","optionReasons":{"D":"An ideal hypnotic acts quickly enough to facilitate sleep, lasts appropriately, preserves sleep architecture and causes minimal residual impairment the following day."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"c4aec116e39b288fc5da06d85dfd43dc0d0a0725ff33c3ec40569aff0d518e75"},"q-ff9261219826":{"correct":"D","answerText":"All of the above","explanation":"Benzodiazepine hypnotics may cause physiological dependence, additive sedation with alcohol or other depressants and next-day residual drowsiness.","optionReasons":{"D":"Benzodiazepine hypnotics may cause physiological dependence, additive sedation with alcohol or other depressants and next-day residual drowsiness."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"6f66a83a7617e606d4669f426a5e013256540f1e66aa0c3d2a53f864d7c71238"},"q-f03295f583ed":{"correct":"C","answerText":"A dose-dependent decrease in both REM and slow wave sleep","explanation":"Benzodiazepine hypnotics generally reduce slow-wave sleep and often suppress REM sleep to varying degrees rather than increasing both components.","optionReasons":{"C":"Benzodiazepine hypnotics generally reduce slow-wave sleep and often suppress REM sleep to varying degrees rather than increasing both components."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"da684e7f112010525094595a2c2f8bc5baa303995021795f6f842c5525488648"},"q-14310a46871c":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Triazolam","explanation":"Short-acting triazolam has a relatively high potential for rebound insomnia when discontinued abruptly, compared with longer-acting compounds.","optionReasons":{"A":"Short-acting triazolam has a relatively high potential for rebound insomnia when discontinued abruptly, compared with longer-acting compounds."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"9b15a9581c6b67456d35428894ee90b1403f45e3a37eafeb596a98133bee760f"},"q-6ae0e865a451":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Zolpidem","explanation":"Zolpidem binds preferentially to alpha-1-associated benzodiazepine receptor sites and enhances GABA-mediated inhibition.","optionReasons":{"B":"Zolpidem binds preferentially to alpha-1-associated benzodiazepine receptor sites and enhances GABA-mediated inhibition."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"b48113f142a28821773e3eb7f9ae71ef643d587054bffbf7f76ad276180012d5"},"q-c0fa45142eac":{"correct":"D","answerText":"All of the above","explanation":"Zolpidem usually causes less disruption of sleep architecture and fewer muscle-relaxant or anticonvulsant effects than traditional benzodiazepines, but dependence and complex sleep behaviors remain possible.","optionReasons":{"D":"Zolpidem usually causes less disruption of sleep architecture and fewer muscle-relaxant or anticonvulsant effects than traditional benzodiazepines, but dependence and complex sleep behaviors remain possible."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"e268aa09c9e67469816a71b98d4d7c97b19209a629359e7de6c702e46447a9d5"},"q-947e72450709":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Thiopental","explanation":"Thiopental is an intravenous barbiturate historically used to induce general anesthesia because of its rapid brain penetration.","optionReasons":{"A":"Thiopental is an intravenous barbiturate historically used to induce general anesthesia because of its rapid brain penetration."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"ff85cb632cc8e1cacaa5a3c6e132e66dee055d71254a7b2faae1e90508519e79"},"q-ce022e0836a3":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Depression of the medullar respiratory center","explanation":"Severe overdose with sedative-hypnotic depressants, particularly barbiturates, can suppress medullary respiratory drive and lead to respiratory failure.","optionReasons":{"A":"Severe overdose with sedative-hypnotic depressants, particularly barbiturates, can suppress medullary respiratory drive and lead to respiratory failure."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"37503b29c37a6cb7cb33c8771a3875234a8c1247ce3c46ba5b5365fca02143ea"},"q-24ce6c77a42a":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Action on the medullar vasomotor center","explanation":"Severe sedative-hypnotic poisoning may depress medullary vasomotor regulation, producing hypotension and circulatory collapse.","optionReasons":{"C":"Severe sedative-hypnotic poisoning may depress medullary vasomotor regulation, producing hypotension and circulatory collapse."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"6d21c077f308147e2a3e22e1a9cd765ac4d435ab74815fba967ab79d4807806a"},"q-e5706767a8a8":{"correct":"D","answerText":"All of the above mechanisms","explanation":"Antiseizure drugs work through multiple mechanisms including enhancement of inhibitory GABA signaling, reduction of excitatory neurotransmission and modulation of sodium or calcium currents.","optionReasons":{"D":"Antiseizure drugs work through multiple mechanisms including enhancement of inhibitory GABA signaling, reduction of excitatory neurotransmission and modulation of sodium or calcium currents."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"7dfa3adc511bc437bb2c8605675caf9666c4f4c67af3b5aab48a2ca7684612d1"},"q-d9266979aeb5":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Phenobarbital","explanation":"Phenobarbital enhances GABA-A receptor-mediated inhibition; ethosuximide primarily inhibits T-type calcium current, whereas carbamazepine acts chiefly at sodium channels.","optionReasons":{"C":"Phenobarbital enhances GABA-A receptor-mediated inhibition; ethosuximide primarily inhibits T-type calcium current, whereas carbamazepine acts chiefly at sodium channels."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"3d1b122bbda29e999d2c0312fecfd4cc3d39599adb65c4832f38847e068f66cf"},"q-d059b6b898f1":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Ethosuximide","explanation":"Ethosuximide reduces low-threshold T-type calcium currents in thalamic neurons, a key mechanism for its efficacy in absence seizures.","optionReasons":{"C":"Ethosuximide reduces low-threshold T-type calcium currents in thalamic neurons, a key mechanism for its efficacy in absence seizures."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"52311ac536acd46e54b2ec2ea54389719dd25d1fce3cc2dec33471781092b39e"},"q-7a205cc37fbb":{"correct":"D","answerText":"All of the above","explanation":"Lamotrigine, carbamazepine and phenytoin all inhibit voltage-gated sodium-channel activity, reducing repetitive neuronal firing by stabilizing inactivated states.","optionReasons":{"D":"Lamotrigine, carbamazepine and phenytoin all inhibit voltage-gated sodium-channel activity, reducing repetitive neuronal firing by stabilizing inactivated states."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"d0c7b396f5832690346173983d3e0ed3e8bd289bc795f32ad0cfc73701f261d7"},"q-dd8ae9699813":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Lamotrigine","explanation":"Lamotrigine reduces presynaptic release of excitatory neurotransmitters, especially glutamate, partly by inhibiting voltage-gated sodium channels.","optionReasons":{"B":"Lamotrigine reduces presynaptic release of excitatory neurotransmitters, especially glutamate, partly by inhibiting voltage-gated sodium channels."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"5c3b5dc00e75d45f70a67ca095e0ac34ff970c3283ca35963b6eb3919812bb87"},"q-8ba774cb3ee4":{"correct":"D","answerText":"All of the above","explanation":"Carbamazepine, phenytoin and valproate have all been used for focal or generalized tonic-clonic seizures, though choice depends on seizure classification and patient-specific safety factors.","optionReasons":{"D":"Carbamazepine, phenytoin and valproate have all been used for focal or generalized tonic-clonic seizures, though choice depends on seizure classification and patient-specific safety factors."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"9f04f0e7a099cf47084ebc73ca2a4537947917ec468349fd1490d99bfd0ce339"},"q-8133488bf662":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Valproate","explanation":"Valproate is effective against absence seizures, whereas carbamazepine and phenytoin can aggravate them. Modern treatment choice must consider reproductive risks and current guidelines.","optionReasons":{"A":"Valproate is effective against absence seizures, whereas carbamazepine and phenytoin can aggravate them. Modern treatment choice must consider reproductive risks and current guidelines."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"86ecea2249b792286ca3d73f2e88a1491f289e43c72ac2ee417000fa4444a181"},"q-1fa18f36b37e":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Clonazepam","explanation":"Clonazepam enhances GABA-A signaling and is effective for many myoclonic seizure syndromes, unlike carbamazepine or phenytoin, which may worsen certain myoclonias.","optionReasons":{"C":"Clonazepam enhances GABA-A signaling and is effective for many myoclonic seizure syndromes, unlike carbamazepine or phenytoin, which may worsen certain myoclonias."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"4875833ed0e6e7116668e7fa5e3065a05f5c4822704c4d1f03ffb2413c177ebd"},"q-4cc613e88efc":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Diazepam","explanation":"Diazepam is a rapid-acting benzodiazepine capable of terminating convulsive status epilepticus. Current adult protocols frequently prefer intravenous lorazepam when available; it is not listed here.","optionReasons":{"C":"Diazepam is a rapid-acting benzodiazepine capable of terminating convulsive status epilepticus. Current adult protocols frequently prefer intravenous lorazepam when available; it is not listed here."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"771545877a7892bcc8b81d63caee1ddd843d038502c3f5551005480c60de4ce7"},"q-691acdea6b1e":{"correct":"A","answerText":"It blocks sodium channels","explanation":"Phenytoin primarily stabilizes inactivated voltage-gated sodium channels, limiting sustained high-frequency neuronal firing.","optionReasons":{"A":"Phenytoin primarily stabilizes inactivated voltage-gated sodium channels, limiting sustained high-frequency neuronal firing."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"7ac23ec853d03fc4bff5003f8585503f08ffbb224a891433ddc937cc8703226c"},"q-253ddd87d28a":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Grand mal epilepsy","explanation":"Phenytoin is effective against generalized tonic-clonic seizures and focal seizures but not typical absence seizures.","optionReasons":{"B":"Phenytoin is effective against generalized tonic-clonic seizures and focal seizures but not typical absence seizures."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"a114db93d23d70d616315942e57cc4e4197f172d8dfadc978857c3b1dccdbaa7"},"q-97f29884b50b":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Gingival hyperplasia","explanation":"Phenytoin can cause gingival overgrowth through changes in gingival connective-tissue turnover; other recognized toxicities include nystagmus and ataxia.","optionReasons":{"C":"Phenytoin can cause gingival overgrowth through changes in gingival connective-tissue turnover; other recognized toxicities include nystagmus and ataxia."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"838be945de3010f535345c38e98f343dad418a7f439e88099d411736d1885145"},"q-73c16d6f0bbd":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Phenytoin","explanation":"Phenytoin induces hepatic drug-metabolizing enzymes and may reduce exposure to other medicines.","optionReasons":{"B":"Phenytoin induces hepatic drug-metabolizing enzymes and may reduce exposure to other medicines."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"f930968c8ef05777688ca6e8fc82e4af4250c769cc3d840e20550bcff4175360"},"q-995217f18fc8":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Carbamazepine","explanation":"Carbamazepine blocks voltage-gated sodium channels and is an established treatment for trigeminal neuralgia.","optionReasons":{"C":"Carbamazepine blocks voltage-gated sodium channels and is an established treatment for trigeminal neuralgia."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"ca5c1fdca3ee8f7ec73187a82f72cdb6d926d125771c27366da2daef649756fd"},"q-57ce284d1ac4":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Diplopia, ataxia, and nausea","explanation":"Carbamazepine dose-related neurological adverse effects commonly include diplopia, dizziness, ataxia and gastrointestinal upset.","optionReasons":{"A":"Carbamazepine dose-related neurological adverse effects commonly include diplopia, dizziness, ataxia and gastrointestinal upset."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"755519f5ce359922b06ca743d2c0117f404f9c7bfb6de617851e77882ac78609"},"q-fc9f606a2eea":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Phenobarbital","explanation":"Phenobarbital prolongs opening of the GABA-A chloride channel; benzodiazepines such as diazepam mainly increase the frequency of opening events.","optionReasons":{"C":"Phenobarbital prolongs opening of the GABA-A chloride channel; benzodiazepines such as diazepam mainly increase the frequency of opening events."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"962af73e6c11f6a6d8ac9157e40beb029c5c64447a338b6554693833840610d1"},"q-b050a04a3b59":{"correct":"D","answerText":"All of the above","explanation":"Phenobarbital can cause sedation, physical dependence and aggravation of absence-type seizures because it does not adequately control typical absence epilepsy.","optionReasons":{"D":"Phenobarbital can cause sedation, physical dependence and aggravation of absence-type seizures because it does not adequately control typical absence epilepsy."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"9af8139bc642ffa0381b932115a7068fec38cb31929df521853a6544ef040b95"},"q-9d8497ae1846":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Lamotrigine","explanation":"Lamotrigine belongs to the phenyltriazine chemical class and reduces neuronal excitability principally via voltage-gated sodium-channel blockade.","optionReasons":{"C":"Lamotrigine belongs to the phenyltriazine chemical class and reduces neuronal excitability principally via voltage-gated sodium-channel blockade."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"41ecec7674fda5f68d24a2c140c47e20026b08caae66b0b9111fea4e47ca7268"},"q-e19bdd84194f":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Vigabatrin","explanation":"Vigabatrin irreversibly inhibits GABA transaminase, reducing GABA breakdown and increasing inhibitory transmitter availability.","optionReasons":{"C":"Vigabatrin irreversibly inhibits GABA transaminase, reducing GABA breakdown and increasing inhibitory transmitter availability."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"4a1ad58556acde1dddef57e4eb93667440e34e676a0d8b45ee32f3980a3a4ff1"},"q-1ea30b82d9c3":{"correct":"D","answerText":"All of the above","explanation":"Topiramate and felbamate exert multiple antiseizure effects involving excitatory glutamate signaling, sodium-channel modulation and inhibitory GABA-related mechanisms.","optionReasons":{"D":"Topiramate and felbamate exert multiple antiseizure effects involving excitatory glutamate signaling, sodium-channel modulation and inhibitory GABA-related mechanisms."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"338e8db372aef8603f8ddf470bd28cffa39c98b1d4ff1ae428c05cd3f6188093"},"q-391d369c5333":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Ethosuximide","explanation":"Ethosuximide is a classic first-line agent for isolated typical absence seizures because it suppresses thalamic T-type calcium currents.","optionReasons":{"B":"Ethosuximide is a classic first-line agent for isolated typical absence seizures because it suppresses thalamic T-type calcium currents."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"93b39d5acb6955f404a1481a5a99b0f41a164e54e584460b5abd1ee616621c45"},"q-5f3130d782a9":{"correct":"D","answerText":"All of the above","explanation":"Valproate has broad-spectrum antiseizure activity against generalized tonic-clonic, absence and myoclonic seizures, although important teratogenic risks constrain its use.","optionReasons":{"D":"Valproate has broad-spectrum antiseizure activity against generalized tonic-clonic, absence and myoclonic seizures, although important teratogenic risks constrain its use."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"5c0293250e83e2528b2c0713a3145f611e35d508332bbdc97c313bd9ca0ec7e2"},"q-6ef0e100e24e":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Valproate","explanation":"Valproate is active against generalized myoclonic seizures; choice in current practice must account carefully for major pregnancy and reproductive risks.","optionReasons":{"A":"Valproate is active against generalized myoclonic seizures; choice in current practice must account carefully for major pregnancy and reproductive risks."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"5bd879a5317cdd3d438cf414b393f80c67c74ed4e32bdc7ce9b905bfedb0ce76"},"q-67b292c963f8":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Zonisamide","explanation":"Zonisamide is a sulfonamide derivative that blocks voltage-gated sodium channels and also inhibits T-type calcium currents.","optionReasons":{"B":"Zonisamide is a sulfonamide derivative that blocks voltage-gated sodium channels and also inhibits T-type calcium currents."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"890b0e0c2b4cde70b84506fd1b9e54c81bee64ecf787e5e363a9a1eac268568b"},"q-f6b0d8d9648f":{"correct":"D","answerText":"Lorazepam","explanation":"Lorazepam is a benzodiazepine that positively modulates GABA-A receptors and is used in seizure emergencies.","optionReasons":{"D":"Lorazepam is a benzodiazepine that positively modulates GABA-A receptors and is used in seizure emergencies."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"9592f70ee82808325de0ccb48ba5bcdd619a186050053739f8217e36de26c82e"},"q-11c1e5103244":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Diazepam","explanation":"Diazepam binds the benzodiazepine-sensitive GABA-A receptor complex, enhancing inhibitory chloride conductance; vigabatrin works indirectly by inhibiting GABA breakdown.","optionReasons":{"B":"Diazepam binds the benzodiazepine-sensitive GABA-A receptor complex, enhancing inhibitory chloride conductance; vigabatrin works indirectly by inhibiting GABA breakdown."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"08900b3f9062dbe05e8e9216b7065cf79b459ee0e825453d66d2ed6d2d93f3ea"},"q-85caa8603e7e":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Tolerance","explanation":"Tolerance can develop to benzodiazepine antiseizure or hypnotic effects, limiting their usefulness as chronic monotherapy for some conditions.","optionReasons":{"A":"Tolerance can develop to benzodiazepine antiseizure or hypnotic effects, limiting their usefulness as chronic monotherapy for some conditions."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"88f226917f233e2a07ece8369484b914aecd87ba271027fde57daaf44bdf0839"},"q-ae460ec1a3df":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Clonazepam","explanation":"Clonazepam is a relatively long-acting benzodiazepine with activity against several absence and myoclonic seizure syndromes.","optionReasons":{"C":"Clonazepam is a relatively long-acting benzodiazepine with activity against several absence and myoclonic seizure syndromes."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"f2323dbf32bd7698b69a1c6158037bff7a7ed552075fe6d09118676b34ceba46"},"q-8fc72322364e":{"correct":"D","answerText":"All of the above","explanation":"Phenytoin, valproate and topiramate are all associated with fetal risks, including increased risks of particular congenital malformations and adverse neurodevelopmental effects.","optionReasons":{"D":"Phenytoin, valproate and topiramate are all associated with fetal risks, including increased risks of particular congenital malformations and adverse neurodevelopmental effects."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"a477324011428c169ade9542ec6a3f1190533fc9f14caaccd37570748f2126e6"},"q-c8712b3685b0":{"correct":"A","answerText":"A selective loss of dopaminergic neurons","explanation":"Parkinson disease is associated with progressive degeneration of dopaminergic neurons in the substantia nigra pars compacta and resultant striatal dopamine deficiency.","optionReasons":{"A":"Parkinson disease is associated with progressive degeneration of dopaminergic neurons in the substantia nigra pars compacta and resultant striatal dopamine deficiency."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"7039d1c9be4636ea6ce654515e5e1f6c603c395e0cc07a56ea78749b52ea8cbb"},"q-59ca7a71cc1e":{"correct":"D","answerText":"All of the above","explanation":"Parkinson motor circuitry is affected by dopaminergic loss and altered relative cholinergic and glutamatergic signaling, so all three transmitter systems contribute.","optionReasons":{"D":"Parkinson motor circuitry is affected by dopaminergic loss and altered relative cholinergic and glutamatergic signaling, so all three transmitter systems contribute."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"e613d951d1060066748c63a6ce23b1118896b6cd49a0eecfbcd4c52f1fb338bf"},"q-480fb406562c":{"correct":"D","answerText":"All of the above","explanation":"Antiparkinsonian therapies restore dopaminergic drive, counterbalance cholinergic tone or modulate excessive glutamatergic signaling through different mechanisms.","optionReasons":{"D":"Antiparkinsonian therapies restore dopaminergic drive, counterbalance cholinergic tone or modulate excessive glutamatergic signaling through different mechanisms."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"39686f7d7d50db4ff1303de418359f0487b54867b62d6ca6a2acc1e700e6fe2d"},"q-4aef2365d41f":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Chlorpromazine","explanation":"Chlorpromazine blocks dopamine D2 receptors and can cause drug-induced parkinsonism; benzodiazepines and carbamazepine do not have this typical dopamine-blocking effect.","optionReasons":{"A":"Chlorpromazine blocks dopamine D2 receptors and can cause drug-induced parkinsonism; benzodiazepines and carbamazepine do not have this typical dopamine-blocking effect."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"d146b32300e39977bd24efec2feacf457da37617c4984522b6f41f25b5ecc2f8"},"q-eb03bd23beea":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Levodopa","explanation":"Levodopa is the immediate metabolic precursor converted to dopamine by aromatic L-amino acid decarboxylase in dopaminergic pathways.","optionReasons":{"B":"Levodopa is the immediate metabolic precursor converted to dopamine by aromatic L-amino acid decarboxylase in dopaminergic pathways."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"63400c8afde477740e7aeb61168776ec13e064f19453b358e1dc2546139a5f85"},"q-dc8182d80730":{"correct":"A","answerText":"Dopamine does not cross the blood-brain barrier","explanation":"Dopamine itself does not cross the blood-brain barrier adequately, whereas levodopa is transported into the brain and then converted to dopamine.","optionReasons":{"A":"Dopamine itself does not cross the blood-brain barrier adequately, whereas levodopa is transported into the brain and then converted to dopamine."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"e49865391a7ae423fa52ffb7fc0fbbfe7bbd2f0c9f47188af8ff872d6ec13554"},"q-52529d290811":{"correct":"C","answerText":"Carbidopa","explanation":"Carbidopa inhibits peripheral aromatic L-amino acid decarboxylase, reducing peripheral levodopa conversion and increasing delivery to the CNS.","optionReasons":{"C":"Carbidopa inhibits peripheral aromatic L-amino acid decarboxylase, reducing peripheral levodopa conversion and increasing delivery to the CNS."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"ead0c2a676d48ad6c43a0bb2f2484bd7ad8ed6ea32c53a1a905ef9ef70720bae"},"q-c31829e73ea4":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Inhibition of dopa decarboxilase","explanation":"Carbidopa inhibits peripheral dopa decarboxylase and thereby reduces levodopa conversion to dopamine before it reaches the brain.","optionReasons":{"B":"Carbidopa inhibits peripheral dopa decarboxylase and thereby reduces levodopa conversion to dopamine before it reaches the brain."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"ac0cae2614cc108a857304744aa1ea94ad3c33846495c4ec9d95b697537e45e7"},"q-514b7292c868":{"correct":"D","answerText":"All of the above","explanation":"Carbidopa reduces peripheral levodopa metabolism, permitting lower doses, higher levodopa availability and reduced peripheral adverse effects when combined with levodopa.","optionReasons":{"D":"Carbidopa reduces peripheral levodopa metabolism, permitting lower doses, higher levodopa availability and reduced peripheral adverse effects when combined with levodopa."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"27719e7a5e060cb994be8a3aaba665641928b236c9fe1febe0886051c3d5e7ba"},"q-2f6a4a40d37e":{"correct":"B","answerText":"Clozapine","explanation":"Clozapine can reduce severe levodopa-associated psychosis with relatively little worsening of motor symptoms because of its unusual receptor-binding profile.","optionReasons":{"B":"Clozapine can reduce severe levodopa-associated psychosis with relatively little worsening of motor symptoms because of its unusual receptor-binding profile."},"references":[],"review":"newly_reasoned_provisional_no_references_2026_10_20","reviewDate":"2026-10-20","provisional":true,"sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"keyVerified":false,"questionTextHash":"4bdbc4304d89cf87baaea3b5061e060df08dc5d0af892aebb691bf5d432c8e41"},"q-d50549703306":{"correct":"D","answer